  @missions {
    MissionService: "CRUD, assign, accept (prerequisite check), complete (bonus tracking), abandon, expire, grantRewards. Emits mission:assigned / mission:accepted / mission:abandoned / mission:failed / objective:updated / mission:completed / mission:expired / mission:feedback. 15-min expiration cron. THREE CLAIMS IN THE OLD TEXT WERE FALSE — all verified 2026-09-24. Claim (2) has since been FIXED (2026-09-24, review pass 3); (1) and (3) remain live defects: (1) THERE IS NO 5-MISSION CAP. gameBalance.MAX_ACTIVE_MISSIONS = 5 (gameBalance.ts:302) has ZERO CALLERS repo-wide and assignMission (missionService.ts:341-400) performs no count check, so nothing limits how many missions a player holds. (2) FIXED 2026-09-24. mission:failed WAS never emitted — a dead LISTENER at index.ts:265 waiting on an event nothing fired. It is now emitted from abandonMission (missionService.ts:705, reason 'abandoned') and the expiry sweep (:1718, reason 'expired'). WAKING IT WAS NOT A NO-OP: the listener calls advanceStory(missionId, 'failed'), which walks the step's failureBranch and can set storyArc.status='failed' PERMANENTLY. Since abandonMission also returns the Mission row to the pool (status 'available', assignedTo null), abandoning a story mission destroyed its arc while leaving the mission takeable. index.ts:265 now branches on reason: 'expired' advances the arc (running out of time is a real failure), 'abandoned' writes only a storyLedger entry. THE LESSON: before emitting an event that has a waiting listener, read what the listener DOES. (3) completeMission has NO $transaction. It is a repository mutate claim-then-pay (missionService.ts:1017-1075); the comment at :1053 says so outright — making the pair genuinely atomic needs both sides in one transaction, which is pass 2's work."
    MissionGeneratorService: "Procedural gen from 39 templates. selectTemplate() deduplication, generateFromTemplate() + RewardScaling, generateAIMission(). Midnight CronJob daily gen. Provisions via ServerContentService."
    MissionIntegrationService: "15 hooks connecting game actions to objectives. Available in CommandContext.services."
    FactionKnowledgeService: "Faction-scoped asset knowledge. addEntry() upserts with confidence. getSnapshot() cached 60s. serializeForPrompt() → KNOWN_TARGETS. expireEntries() + decayConfidence(0.05, min 0.1)."
    StoryMissionService: "AI multi-step narrative arcs. createStoryArc() → 3-7 steps with branching. advanceStory() on complete/fail. Adapted steps on failure. Injects ServerContentService."
    KeyFragmentService: "Key Fragment Discovery & Endgame Engine (1202 lines, recounted 2026-09-24). Full lifecycle: CLAIM (unclaimed fragments), STEAL (hack from other players), TRANSFER (voluntary trade), PROGRESS (recompute from holdings), UNLOCK (one player holds all 9), ENDGAME (final choice + narrative), HINTS (contextual). 9 fragments: 3 types × 3 (Sword, Key, Collar). Fragments UNIQUE — one holder at a time. All ownership mutations (claim/steal/transfer) wrapped in Prisma $transaction for atomicity. Endgame choices: help (free AIDA), expose (broadcast locations), exploit (bind AIDA). Extends EventEmitter."

    @architecture_doc {
      read_first: "MISSIONS_ARCHITECTURE.md — full read of the mission system (2026-08-31). Read it before touching missions."
      dual_state: "Mission table (definition) + PlayerProgress.missionProgress JSON (per-player progress). Offers are PER PLAYER — missionGenerator writes each generated mission into that player's own blob as 'available'. NOT an anonymous global pool: treating it as one breaks level scaling and lets two players complete the same mission."
      producers: "9 code paths create missions. 6 never write the blob, so AI-persona and admin-panel missions are unreachable by the player."
      unwinnable: "~15 of 39 templates were impossible before Tier 1."
    }

    @tier1_fixes {
      status: "DONE 2026-08-31. Gate harness 15/15, U1 11/11, verify-mission-provisioning 5/5."
      M11: "hackService passed targetId (target USER id) into onHackComplete, where missionIntegration compares it against objective.metadata.serverId. GameServer.id === User.id is never true → hack_target unwinnable in every case across 7 templates. Now passes targetServerId (was in scope, unused) and the hook param is renamed so the name cannot invite the bug again. SIDE EFFECT: install_backdoor + breach_server got STRICTER — they only 'passed' before because an unbound matchesEntity returns true for ANY server."
      M12: "readFile now returns nodeId; both download call sites pass the real source file id instead of \"\". Their (missionIntegration as any) casts were typed at the same time — that same cast pattern had hidden an arity bug earlier."
      M13: "The provisioning GATE and the switch (obj.type) inside provisionMissionInfrastructure had drifted: 3 case arms were unreachable. Gate is now a single exported PROVISIONED_OBJECTIVE_TYPES (15 types) and scripts/verify-mission-provisioning.ts asserts gate↔switch parity by parsing the source."
      M14: "Fixed by AUTHORING intent, not the registry: install_backdoor was authored as a count in 4/5 templates (1,1,1,2) while registered boolean → became count, hook now increments. decode_content was boolean in 9/10 → its lone numeric target was corrected instead. 134/134 objectives now agree with progressType."
      trap_full_validation: "Promoting ALL validateObjective failures to a throw rejects 49 of 134 template objectives, because required metadata (serverId/fileId/...) is legitimately absent until provisionMissionInfrastructure backfills it. Only the target/progressType mismatch is knowable at authoring time — validate that, debug-log the rest."
      world_inflation: "Mission provisioning MINTS a target server when it cannot find a suitable one. A handful of harness runs took the DB from 38 → 114 servers with 40 content jobs queued. connect awaits contentQueue.ensureReady(), so a deep queue is felt by players as a slow connect. Reuse before minting."
      remaining: "M3 AND M4 ARE BOTH CLOSED — verified 2026-09-24. M4 (timeLimit 1000x unit mismatch) was closed by server/src/utils/missionTime.ts, the single conversion point for the seconds unit (commit 4a33a0c). M3 (isBonus wrongly in the completion gate) was closed at missionService.ts:1098-1105, where requiredObjectives filters !o.isBonus so bonus objectives no longer block completion (commit c8f6216). ACTUALLY REMAINING: Tier 2 — M16 (skillPoints/unlocks displayed, never granted: 13 and 2 templates), M17 (reputation always credits repNeutral). Tier 3 — M2 (all-or-nothing blob write-back; still the reason generated offers do not reach players)."
    }
  }

  @session_handoff_2026_09_01 {
    read_first: "PLAN.md (phase order + decisions log), PHASE1_AUDIT.md, VERIFY.md. Committed as a75383d (33 files, +2045/-569) on branch `test`. Docs and server/scripts/ are gitignored BY MAINTAINER DECISION — single machine, dev-only."

    phase3_gate: "GATE PASSED 2026-09-23 with ONE leg open. The 09-01 gate text asked for concurrency 'by hand, two browser tabs'; that is now covered by harnesses that do strictly more — each drives the real service with Promise.all AND carries a negative control reproducing the old failure, which two tabs cannot do. Its three named legs map exactly onto shipped harnesses (exact-credit double-spend -> progress-repo, same-fragment crack -> d6-race, fragment.crack past 100 -> progress-repo). PROVISIONING-FROM-EMPTY was verified on a THROWAWAY database (createdb aida_gate_scratch -> db push --force-reset -> 70 tables, 4 Phase 3 tables, 18 FKs, 5 uniques, 10 D9 indexes, then dropped) rather than by wiping the dev DB — same property proven, 134 users and the D3 backfill preserved. STILL OPEN, owner MAINTAINER: `npm run db:reset` end-to-end, because running prisma/seed.ts is blocked in this environment by the same safety check D2 hit. The db push half IS proven; only the seed is unobserved."

    where_we_are: "Phase 0 done. Phase 1 done + audited + its 4 P0s fixed. Phase 2 DONE. PHASE 3 STEPS 1-4 ALL DONE 2026-09-23 (@phase3_steps_1_2, @phase3_progress_repo, @phase3_d3_pass1, @phase3_d7_upserts) — schema constraints/indexes/FKs/R8/K tables, D10 connections, D6, PlayerProgressRepository, D3 both passes, and D7's upsert conversion. The three N+1s are CLOSED. STILL OPEN in Phase 3 and nothing else: take limits on unbounded findMany (deferred on the same measurement argument as the indexes), D4's CHECK constraint and the FileSystemNode partial root index (BOTH deferred to migration adoption by decision — raw SQL would be dropped by the next db push --force-reset). THE PHASE 3 GATE IS REWRITTEN AND PASSED except one maintainer-owned leg (`npm run db:reset` end-to-end) — see phase3_gate above. Phase 3 is effectively CLOSED; next is Phase 4 (Security)."

    decisions_11_to_14: "11 = strict phase order, do not pull later phases forward. 12 = U3c redesign: under-skilled attempts must be HARDER + RISKIER + REWARDED, which needs a minigame/process/resource-cost per command — only `sweep` and `hack` have all three, so the rest is Phase 8/9 feature work. 13 = split O4: CI now (cannot rot, value peaks during churny phases), Docker at go-live (pins build output Phase 7 will churn). 14 = migrations adopted at go-live only."

    THE_PATTERN: "Every single defect found in Phases 1-2 was invisible to tsc/eslint/svelte-check AND to the static contract check. Each was one of: (a) a SECOND CODE PATH the fix did not reach, (b) an ENFORCEMENT LAYER that silently excluded the fix, or (c) TWO CORRECT CHANGES CANCELLING each other. None is visible in the fix's own diff. When closing any phase, ask 'where else does this pattern live?' — that question found all of them."

    my_false_claims_this_session: "FIVE documented claims of mine turned out false: (1) migrations were rebuilt with a 0001_init baseline — there is NO migrations directory at all; (2) M11 made install_backdoor/breach_server 'stricter' — they are not in PROVISIONED_OBJECTIVE_TYPES so matchesEntity still matches ANY server; (3) G6 'all sites route through matchesEntity' — five bypassed it; (4) 'all five soft commands gate on hacking' — there are six, analyze is forensics; (5) S20 reseeding would throw on the FK — seed.ts deletes inventoryItem first. LESSON: I repeatedly recorded an INTENTION as an OUTCOME. Verify before writing it down as done."

    my_harnesses_lie_too: "Four times a harness of mine reported a defect that did not exist: role cached at auth so a DB promotion did not apply; a 1.5s wait against a 10s background process; driving `scan` when the emit lives in the subnet-sweep branch; and a regex reporting three phantom failures. A FAILURE needs the same scrutiny as a pass. Also: an empty grep is not a finding — check the working directory and use a positive control."

    phase2_runtime_found_3_real_defects: "Running VERIFY.md §5 found what every static check passed clean: (1) setSocketIO() had ZERO callers on serverService AND missionService — 21 stranded emits including player:levelup, which the client answers with a sound + urgent notification that had NEVER fired; fixed by injecting SOCKET_IO rather than adding the missing setter call. (2) discoverServers() is reachable only from a dead no-resource fallback branch. (3) The live subnet sweep emitted server:subnet-scan — a name no client listens for, and one check-socket-contract.ts could not SEE because its regex excluded hyphens (12 events invisible). Unified onto server:discovered. All three layers had to be fixed before one notification worked. FOLLOW-UP 2026-09-24: the dead setSocketIO-style setters were NOT all removed — zero-caller setters still sit at serverService.ts:164, missionService.ts:181 and missionIntegration.ts:177. Delete them rather than leaving the trap (CLAUDE.md bug shape #4)."

    verify_md_caveat: "VERIFY.md §5.1 drives `report mission` to credit an explore objective, because that fires onServerConnect WITHOUT a link — the explore-farming defect filed to Phase 5. Real `connect` needs adjacency. WHEN PHASE 5 FIXES THAT, §5.1 BREAKS and will look like a reward-bridge regression. Switch it to genuine connects then."

    phase3_state: "Gate REWRITTEN (the original demanded `prisma migrate deploy`, impossible with no migrations). D7 uniques LANDED on InventoryItem(userId,shopItemId) and FileSystemNode(serverId,parentId,name), applied via db push and PROVEN to reject P2002 with a positive control. A real duplicate was merged first: two /home dirs created in the SAME SECOND on an AI-provisioned server — concurrent provisioning, check whether serverContentService can provision one server twice. CAVEAT: parentId is nullable and Postgres treats NULLs as distinct, so two same-named ROOT nodes are still possible; would need a partial index. D4 (credits >= 0 CHECK) SHOULD NOT be done as raw SQL — with migrations deferred, the next db push --force-reset drops it silently; do it with migration adoption or rely on PlayerProgressRepository.spendCredits. D7's upsert conversion is still open — those sites now THROW P2002 instead of creating duplicates."

    open_gates: "CI has NEVER run on GitHub (validated locally only; npm ci on a clean runner is the likely divergence). verify-tutorial-altpath gave 10/11 once under back-to-back load, 11/11 on three isolated runs — contention-sensitive, recorded rather than dismissed as flaky."
  }

  @phase3_steps_1_2 {
    read_first: "PLAN.md Phase 3. Harnesses (gitignored, local): server/scripts/verify-phase3-schema.ts 18/18, verify-phase3-d6-fragment-race.ts 8/8, fix-dangling-connections.ts (idempotent data repair)."

    THE_HEADLINE: "TWICE the live data contradicted the audit, and measuring first changed the fix. (1) D10 said currentConnections over-counts; it was 0 on servers holding 33-38 active rows — UNDER-counting — because there are TWO writers with incompatible models and the one that wins is amnesiac. (2) The dominant defect was not in the audit at all: 95 of 95 ServerConnection rows were active with disconnectedAt null on every one, because `connect <ip>` never closed the row for the server being left. Measure before escalating, and measure before BELIEVING the framing too."

    D10_connections: "THREE faults. (a) connectPlayerToServer calls disconnectPlayerFromServer, but that is gameStateManager's IN-MEMORY session only — serverService.disconnectFromServer is the sole writer of the ROWS and is reached only from `disconnect` and `connect home`. So ordinary traversal leaked one active row per hop, forever. connectToServer now deactivates the player's other active rows (session.currentServerId is singular and there is no per-terminal connect, so one-server-at-a-time is the right invariant). (b) currentConnections had serverService's {increment:1} delta AND gameStateManager's absolute `= serverState.activeConnections` running on the SAME connect; the absolute one runs last and wins, and serverStates is an in-memory Map empty after every boot — hence the stored 0. Both now derive from a COUNT of the rows. NOTE it is display-only: maxConnections is not enforced anywhere, only rendered as `current/max`. (c) fragmentCommands.ts:324 was findFirst({userId, isActive:true}) with NO serverId and NO orderBy — safe only with one active row, and players had three — so `fragment.steal` could run against a server the player had left, carrying THAT server's accessLevel past the >=5 gate. Now bound to session.currentServerId. VERIFIED AGAINST REAL TRAFFIC: after verify-tutorial-altpath (4-server hop) each of 7 harness users shows 3 hops / 1 active connection, 0 users with >1, 0 drift across 166 servers, positive control 61 rows with fresh disconnectedAt."

    D10_dont_touch_the_historical_reads: "networkTopologyService:732/:754 ('previously hacked') and playerInfoCommands:984 filter accessLevel > 0 WITHOUT isActive. That is DELIBERATE — a hack you did stays done — so deactivating stale rows does not revoke it. The repair script asserts it (95 -> 95 rows with accessLevel > 0). Do not 'tidy' those into isActive checks."

    D6_fixed_in_the_shared_helper: "changeFragmentOwnership is shared by claim AND steal AND transfer, so all three had the identical read-then-blind-write — the audit only named claim. New expectedHolderId param (null / victim / sender) goes into an updateMany WHERE = compare-and-set; loser matches 0 rows, then re-reads and re-runs the CALLER'S validate so they get 'currently held by X' instead of a generic error. NEGATIVE-TESTED: removing the CAS reproduced the audit exactly — 2 winners, 2 discovery records, loser's StoryProgress counter inflated to 1. Restored and diffed byte-for-byte against a backup."

    R8_the_inert_warning_was_wrong: "PLAN.md said landing skillPoints without Phase 8's economy 'leaves it inert'. True of the ECONOMY, false of the BUG: darknetDungeonService spreads skillPoints:{increment} into the SAME data object as experience, so the missing column threw and safeExecute ate the XP with it. Proven at runtime by replaying the exact statement — 0->5000 XP and 0->2 SP on a real row. Still the ONLY Prisma write of the field; missionService:1091 and storyMissionService:368 build plain JS objects and :1172/missionCommands:416 only render strings."

    D10_FKs_the_audit_was_wrong_about_user_deletion: "Audit said 'no code deletes a User today'. FALSE — prisma/npcOwnership.ts:201 deletes duplicate NPC accounts during identity reconciliation and prisma/seed.ts:499 does user.deleteMany(). That is why onDelete is Cascade and not the default Restrict, which would have turned the NPC merge into a hard failure. Bounty keeps claimedByUserId/serverId as SetNull so a bounty survives losing its claimer. Checked 0 orphans across all 7 columns BEFORE adding; every FK proven to reject with P2003 plus a positive control."

    D9_why_only_nine_indexes: "A full survey of all 56 models found ~70 candidate missing indexes. Only 9 were added (3 on Mission, 6 elsewhere) because THE DATABASE IS TINY: audit_logs 1294 rows, file_system_nodes 221, missions 216, users 91, nothing else over 70. At that size an index is write overhead with no measurable read benefit, and 70 would be churn Phase 7 has to carry. Took only tables that grow WITHOUT BOUND on per-command/per-connect paths. GameEvent had NO index at all and is sorted on every socket connect. Also recorded: several hot predicates are NOT indexable as written — mode:'insensitive' lookups defeat their own @unique btree (aliasCommands:132, fragmentCommands:281, referenceValidationService:78/619), startsWith on homeIp/ipAddress is a LIKE scan, hackCommands:736 ORs against an unindexed `name`. And backdoorService.cleanupExpired / eventService.getEventsByType / getGlobalEvents have ZERO callers — indexing them would index dead code."

    my_harness_lied_again: "verify-phase3-schema reported a FAIL for an FK that psql had just proven rejects correctly. Cause: `e.message.split('\\n')[0]` — PRISMA ERROR MESSAGES START WITH A NEWLINE, so that yields an empty string and every error read as falsy. Now matches on the Prisma `code` (P2003/P2002) and takes the first NON-EMPTY line. The tell was an empty detail field on the failure. ALSO: a boot-wait loop reported 'server up after 1s' using `curl -s -o /dev/null` — which exits 0 on a 404, and there IS no /api/health route. It was accidentally right. A pass needs the same scrutiny as a fail."

    still_open_in_phase3: "STALE HEAD, corrected 2026-09-24: D7's check-then-create -> upsert conversion is DONE (architectInterventionExecutor.ts:704-712) and this entry is superseded on that point by @phase3_d7_upserts. The N+1s (fileService ls, serverContentService boot provisioning, missionService expiry sweep). take limits on unbounded findMany. D4's credits>=0 CHECK stays deferred — raw SQL would be dropped by the next db push --force-reset, so it lands with migration adoption or relies on PlayerProgressRepository.spendCredits. Then steps 3 (PlayerProgressRepository, 27 writers) and 4 (D3 missionProgress blob)."
  }

  @phase3_code_review {
    read_first: "PLAN.md decisions 15 and 16. Review run 2026-09-23 on the full uncommitted diff (4186 lines, 32 files + 2 new repositories), 8 finder angles at high effort."

    THE_RESULT: "NINE REAL BUGS, every one in code already reported as verified with green harnesses. Nine fixed, one pre-existing left to Phase 5. This is the evidence for decision 15 (review between every phase): harnesses structurally cannot find this class."

    THE_DOMINANT_SHAPE: "FOUR of the nine were 'I fixed one half of a pair and left the other' — copyNode got a P2002 handler but moveNode did not; the credit check became conditional SQL but the stack cap stayed a stale JS read; the joined server's connection count was resynced but the abandoned one was not; the `if (progress)` branch moved to the repository but the `else` branch still wrote the dead blob. A test of the half that works PASSES. Same family as verification-lessons' 'second code path the fix did not reach'."

    worst_finding: "incrementObjective skipped the per-user lock while writeMission writes currentCount ABSOLUTELY, so any count credit landing inside a concurrent mutate was erased. REPRODUCED: a +7 during a concurrent boolean update left current_count at 0. Widest window is missionGenerator.mutateAll, which rewrites every mission a player owns. This is the exact lost-update class D3 pass 2 was built to close, reopened via the one unlocked path. Fixed by taking the lock; pinned by a regression assertion in verify-phase3-d3-mission-lock (now 23/23)."

    i_contradicted_my_own_docstrings: "connectToServer's comment claimed the derived count 'cannot drift' while the code never resynced the server being LEFT — a permanent phantom occupant. Check claims against code, including claims written minutes earlier. Second instance this session (the earlier one was 'traceService has no floor', which it does)."

    two_from_my_own_reordering: "completeMission lost its payability guard, so claim-then-pay could burn a mission with rewards unpaid and unretryable. And assertPositiveInt threw on ZERO where the old relative Prisma update was a harmless no-op — a zero-reward bounty was claimed and THEN the grant threw (bounty burned), and darknet grants amounts from AI-authored JSON where a fractional value threw inside safeExecute and paid nothing silently: the exact failure R8 was written to end. Zero/fractional now tolerated, negative still throws."

    totalXP_defect_FIXED: "CLOSED — verified 2026-09-24, do not re-file. personaMissionGenService no longer reads a non-existent `totalXP` column: :226-246 reads m.user.progress?.experience and derives the level through levelForExperience(), so faction mission difficulty now scales to the real player level. The sibling defect named in the same original entry — hackService's 3-arg initiateTrace call — is ALSO fixed (see @phase3_progress_repo). HISTORY, kept for the pattern only: the bug was hidden by `as any`, the FOURTH instance of that pattern concealing a real bug here, after onFactionServerHacked and the (missionIntegration as any) casts."

    deferred_efficiency: "mutateAll rewrites every mission a player owns rather than the keys the callback touched; writeMission costs ~K+6 sequential round trips per objective tick on the hottest path; the backfill script duplicates splitValues/toDate wholesale. Real, all non-correctness, none worth churning before Phase 7."
  }

  @phase3_d7_upserts {
    read_first: "PLAN.md Phase 3 D7. Done 2026-09-23."

    the_count_and_the_real_work: "PLAN.md called architectInterventionExecutor.ts:705 'the known one'. There were 39: 7 inventoryItem + 32 fileSystemNode. All 7 inventory and 17 filesystem sites converted. THE WORK WAS CLASSIFICATION, NOT CONVERSION — a duplicate is not always something to merge. MERGE where re-running is the intent (provisioning, content injection, dungeon regeneration, reward grants — these re-run by design). ERROR where the player must know: touch/mkdir/cp now report FILE_EXISTS/DIRECTORY_EXISTS/DESTINATION_EXISTS on a lost race instead of a generic failure, because an upsert there would silently overwrite a file nobody asked to replace. `cp` had NO name check at all, so it was creating silent duplicates before the constraint existed."

    two_player_visible_defects_found_by_classifying: "(1) defenseCommands decoys CHARGED AND FAILED: decoy names are fixed strings (admin_passwords.db among them) and the cleanup only removes rows already marked isDecoy, so a genuine downloaded file of that name collided; no try/catch there OR in either caller, so the P2002 became 'Command execution failed' AFTER purchaseDefense had committed the 5000c charge in its own transaction. (2) serverContentService's BARE CATCH was building the duplicate roots — written to mean 'FileService is not registered' but it swallowed every failure, so a part-way initializeFileSystem was misread as 'DI unavailable' and execution fell through to the standalone path, which built a SECOND root. The unique index cannot catch that. Both fixed."

    roots_need_a_different_mechanism: "@@unique([serverId, parentId, name]) does NOT cover roots — parentId is null and Postgres treats NULLs as distinct — AND Prisma types the compound's parentId as NON-NULLABLE, so upserting a root on that key is impossible. The two provisioning paths that matter (fileService.initializeFileSystem, serverContentService.ensureBaseFilesystem) now give the root a DETERMINISTIC id `root_<serverId>` so the PRIMARY KEY does the work: a concurrent creator collides there and resolves to the existing row. No schema change, and the preceding findFirst still handles pre-existing cuid roots."

    deliberately_not_converted: "routes/auth.ts x4 — one $transaction against a server created two statements earlier, every parent brand new, collision unreachable. adminApi/servers:267 and contentDraftService:324 — already surface as 409 UNIQUE_CONSTRAINT via formatServerError, which is RIGHT: an admin creating/approving a colliding name should see the conflict. 5 darknet roots + contentDraftService:239 + personaService:944 — all roots, all findFirst-guarded, all on transient dungeon/draft servers inside safeExecute. RESIDUAL HAZARD, recorded: the real fix is a partial unique index on (serverId, name) WHERE parent_id IS NULL, which needs raw SQL — so like D4's CHECK it lands WITH MIGRATION ADOPTION, not as a db execute the next `db push --force-reset` would silently drop."

    a_regex_nearly_botched_it: "A scripted pass to convert all 5 darknet roots matched only 2 of 5 (differing indentation). The assertion `assert n == 5` fired BEFORE the write, so nothing was corrupted. Assert the expected count in every scripted multi-site edit — without it this would have silently converted 2 and left 3, which is worse than converting none."

    my_own_harness_bug_again: "The pass-2 patch to verify-tutorial-altpath left a reference to `objectives2`, a variable that never existed (the real one is `hackObjectives`). All 11 assertions still passed, then it threw AFTER them — so the batch runner showed a blank score and only running it alone revealed the cause. Same lesson as before: read the actual output, do not infer from a missing summary line."
  }

  @phase3_d3_pass1 {
    read_first: "PLAN.md Phase 3 D3. server/src/repositories/playerMissionRepository.ts. Harness: server/scripts/verify-phase3-d3-mission-lock.ts 11/11."

    scope: "64 touchpoints across 7 files (missionService 37, tutorialService 7, storyMissionService 7, missionGenerator 7, aiAgentTools 3, missionCommands 2, auth 1). UNLIKE the PlayerProgressRepository work there was NO SEAM — every site inlined `(progress.missionProgress as any) || {}` and rewrote the WHOLE blob. PASS 1 IS NOW COMPLETE: all 64 converted. What still touches missionProgress directly is THREE ROW CREATIONS (auth.ts:103, missionService.ts:407, tutorialService.ts:998) plus comments — creation is PlayerProgress's concern and has no blob to race with."

    races_closed_per_method: "checkExpiredMissions (the headline — see the_sweep_fix_has_TWO_halves). completeMission = THE DOUBLE-REWARD SITE: the 'already completed' guard and the status flip were separate steps, so the sweep's stale write reverted completed->active and the guard then passed a SECOND time and paid again; now one atomic claim, so exactly one caller can transition and therefore exactly one can pay. Ordered claim-then-pay deliberately: D5's downside (crash => complete but unpaid) is real but strictly better than pay-first, which is repeatable and therefore exploitable. acceptMission: two concurrent accepts both saw 'available', both wrote 'active', and the second also reset startedAt, MOVING THE EXPIRY WINDOW. missionGenerator: the worst stale snapshot in the codebase — merged into a `progress` read taken before the template loop AND minutes of AI generation, wiping everything the player did meanwhile; mutateAll re-reads inside the lock. Plus updateObjective, abandonMission, expireMission, isObjectiveCompleted, getPlayerMissions, assignMission, tutorialService, storyMissionService, aiAgentTools."

    reentrancy_guard_and_the_mistake_that_shaped_it: "The mutex is NOT reentrant: a callback calling back in waits on a lock it already holds = permanent hang for that player, no error, no log. Every callback is synchronous today but nothing enforced it, so there is now a guard that THROWS. IT MUST BE AsyncLocalStorage, NOT a Set of held users — my first version used a Set and THIS CLASS'S OWN HARNESS CAUGHT IT, failing the expiry-sweep test, because a Set cannot distinguish re-entry from a legitimately QUEUED concurrent caller, which is the entire point of the queue. AsyncLocalStorage propagates down the callback's async context and no further, which is exactly the needed distinction."

    deferred_to_pass_2_CLOSED: "BOTH DEFERRED ITEMS ARE CLOSED — verified 2026-09-24: findExpired is indexed (playerMissionRepository.ts:524) and incrementObjective is a relative update (:436). Superseded by pass_2_closed_both_deferred_items below. HISTORY: (1) userIdsWithMissions() was only a PARTIAL fix to the sweep's unbounded read — narrower select, but still reads every player's blob and filters in JS, because 'has an expired active mission' is not expressible as a Prisma predicate over a JSON map keyed by mission id. (2) updateObjective's callers pass an ABSOLUTE value computed from a `current` THEY read (missionIntegration.ts:255,565,570), so their read is outside the lock and two concurrent counters for the SAME objective can still collapse into one. NO LOCK HERE CAN REACH THAT — it needs a relative increment, i.e. pass 2's conditional updates."

    blob_shape_measured: "From the live DB, not the type: 89/101 players hold missions, max 6 each, max 3.6KB. 285 mission entries with missionId/userId/status/startedAt/objectives (202 also expiresAt/completedAt). 415 objectives with id/type/target/current/completed/description (+metadata on 326). Statuses actually in use: active 181, available 75, completed 29 — no 'failed'/'expired' rows exist today even though the code writes them."

    why_two_passes: "A direct swap to tables would change storage AND 64 call sites at once, with every intermediate state having TWO SOURCES OF TRUTH. Pass 1 = repository over the EXISTING blob (pure refactor, no schema change) which gives the blob one writer and closes the races. Pass 2 = swap the repository's internals to PlayerMission + PlayerMissionObjective and backfill; blast radius is one file."

    lock_is_a_QUEUE_not_the_sessionLocks_pattern: "PLAN.md suggested extending gameStateManager's sessionLocks. DO NOT — that pattern REJECTS when contended, and rejecting a contended mission update silently drops a reward, which is the defect rather than the fix. mutate/mutateAll chain per user via `previous.then(fn, fn)` so a contender WAITS; then(fn,fn) specifically so one caller's rejection cannot deadlock everyone queued behind it, and the stored tail never rejects. The chain map deletes its entry when it drains (checked by the harness) so it cannot leak one entry per player the way memoryService's maps do."

    the_sweep_fix_has_TWO_halves: "checkExpiredMissions loaded every player's blob with a bare findMany() (no where/select/take, FOUR json blobs per player) and then, per player, awaited an audit-log write AND a mission.update BEFORE writing its copy back. Half 1: the read-modify-write is now one critical section. HALF 2, equally important: the side effects (socket emit, audit log, mission row) MOVED OUT of that section — they are what made the window two round trips wide. A lock alone would have serialised a still-wide window."

    negative_controls_reproduce_the_double_reward: "The harness's two negative controls run the OLD inline shape and still break: a concurrent pair leaves m1=active — the completion ENTIRELY LOST, which is precisely the audit's 'sweep writes its stale copy, reverting status to active, so the already-completed guard passes again and rewards are granted repeatedly' — and the old sweep overwrites a player's `completed` with `expired`. Without these the 9 positive assertions could have passed merely because the harness failed to interleave."

    PASS_2_DONE: "Storage is PlayerMission + PlayerMissionObjective. The repository's external contract is UNCHANGED, so pass 2 touched no caller — which is what the two-pass split bought. Schema note: target/current are split into TYPED columns (targetCount/currentCount, targetFlag/currentFlag, defensive *Text) rather than Json, and that is load-bearing — a numeric column is what makes the relative increment expressible. Which pair is live is decided by the runtime type of target, mirroring G1. `position` preserves the authored order the array gave for free."

    the_FK_found_a_real_problem: "78 of 299 blob entries (26%) pointed at Mission rows that NO LONGER EXISTED. All 78 were `active`, none completed, and all were ALREADY non-functional — completeMission calls getMission first and throws 'Mission not found', so they could never progress. Backfill skips and REPORTS them rather than dropping silently; onDelete: Cascade means the class cannot accumulate again. Migrated 221 missions / 316 objectives, idempotent, round-trip asserted. The blob is deliberately NOT cleared — reversible fallback."

    pass_2_closed_both_deferred_items: "(1) findExpired is now `where: {status:'active', expiresAt:{lt:now}}` against @@index([status, expiresAt]) — one query where pass 1 scanned every player. (2) incrementObjective is a single `UPDATE ... SET current_count = current_count + n` with completion recomputed in the same statement (sticky per G1); the 11 missionIntegration creditObjective call sites (12 repo-wide; recounted 2026-09-24 — not ~18) that computed `objective.current + n` from a read outside the lock now pass a DELTA to a new missionService.creditObjective. MEASURED by the harness negative control: the old absolute-from-a-read shape lands 1 OF 25 concurrent credits — a 96% loss rate under contention, worse than the audit implied, and nothing a lock around the write could recover."

    TWO_HARNESSES_BROKE_AND_NEITHER_WAS_A_REGRESSION: "verify-tutorial-altpath went 11/11 -> 10/11 and verify-gate-phase1 started erroring. BOTH were reaching behind the app's API: they seeded missions by writing playerProgress.missionProgress directly and read results back from it, so a storage change broke them for reasons unrelated to what they assert. Both now go through the repository like the game does; both green again (11/11, 15/15). LESSON: a harness coupled to STORAGE tests the storage, not the behaviour. And the first instinct — 'tutorial is flaky under back-to-back load', which @session_handoff_2026_09_01 even licensed — would have buried a real signal. Run it alone and read the FAIL before believing the folklore."

    gate: "verify-phase3-d3-mission-lock.ts 13/13 with negative controls that still reproduce the old loss. Full suite green against a live server INCLUDING verify-tutorial-altpath 11/11, which drives objective crediting end-to-end over real sockets — that is the one that would catch a broken conversion. Boot clean: 0 error lines, 0 reentrancy errors."
  }

  @phase3_progress_repo {
    read_first: "server/src/repositories/playerProgressRepository.ts (the file documents each defect it closes). Harness: server/scripts/verify-phase3-progress-repo.ts 26/26."

    the_count_was_wrong: "PLAN.md said 27 distinct writers. There were 43 write sites across 22 files. 24 moved onto the repository. The 19 left are deliberate and each was read to confirm: 10 are missionProgress blob writes (D3/step 4), 4 create the row, 3 are outside its remit (admin arbitrary edit, backup restore's whole-row splat, the achievements array), 2 are increments added with a comment saying why (repNeutral, skillPoints). ALWAYS recount the plan's numbers."

    design_rule: "Every mutation is ONE statement whose correctness does not depend on a value read earlier. spendCredits puts the balance test in the WHERE of the decrement, so the rowcount IS the authorization result. addSkill clamps with GREATEST(0, LEAST(100, col + delta)) INSIDE the UPDATE — the clamp reads the row version it writes — with the column name from a closed whitelist map that doubles as the injection guard for the one interpolation raw SQL needs. addExperience increments and returns, then raises level only `where: {level: {lt: newLevel}}`, so it is monotonic and a racing grant cannot lower it. All methods take an optional tx: a caller already inside $transaction MUST pass it or the statement runs on another connection, outside their transaction, and their atomicity is imaginary."

    shopService_comment_was_a_lie: "shopService's purchase had `// Re-check credits inside transaction to prevent race conditions` over a findUnique. A plain SELECT in a READ COMMITTED transaction takes NO ROW LOCK, so it never prevented anything. The comment is why nobody looked again. Replaced by spendCredits(userId, totalCost, tx)."

    level_had_ONE_writer: "NOT IN THE AUDIT. PlayerProgress.level was raised by exactly one code path — missionService.grantRewards — and otherwise only ever set to 1 at row creation. XP from hackService, darknetDungeonService, messageEncryptionService and fileAccessCommands never recomputed it, so a player who only hacked would accumulate experience and stay level 1 forever, which gates their CPU/RAM/bandwidth, mission difficulty band and shop requiredLevel. MEASURED BEFORE ESCALATING: it has never bitten — highest real XP in the DB is 80, level 2 needs 100, and 0 players are behind their implied level (every non-level-1 row is a harness player levelled by a script). Also deduplicated calculateLevel, which had two identical private copies (missionService + missionGenerator), into one exported levelForExperience."

    correction_to_my_own_note: "Earlier this same session I wrote that traceService's stealth decrement 'had no floor'. IT DOES — Math.min(2, progress.stealth). It is racy in the same way as the caps (JS arithmetic over an earlier read), not unfloored. Corrected in the repository doc comment. Read the line before characterising it."

    negative_controls_are_the_whole_test: "A concurrency harness that cannot interleave passes every invariant for the wrong reason. So the harness runs the OLD patterns too and asserts they STILL BREAK: read-then-spend lands on -200 credits and the JS-computed cap lands on hacking 101 — the audit's exact numbers. Without those two the other 24 assertions would have been meaningless."

    initiateTrace_arity_FIXED: "CLOSED — verified 2026-09-24, do not re-file to Phase 5. hackService.ts:2013-2018 now passes ALL FOUR arguments (attackerId, targetUserId, serverId, evidenceLevel), and the resolve is a TYPED getService<TraceService>(TRACE_SERVICE) at :2002 rather than getService<any>. Both line numbers in the original entry had drifted (:1973 -> :2013, the correct sibling :1270 -> :1277). HISTORY: the call passed THREE args against a FOUR-parameter signature (targetId, initiatedBy, serverId, evidenceLevel), so serverId received the evidence level and evidenceLevel was undefined; ActiveTrace.serverId has a FK to GameServer which rejected it. Seen in the boot log as `Failed to initiate trace {\"serverId\":100}` — 100 is the evidence level. That trace countermeasure has NEVER worked. Survived because the call site is getService<any>(TRACE_SERVICE) — the THIRD recorded instance of `any` erasing a signature here, after onFactionServerHacked and the (missionIntegration as any) casts. The sibling at :1277 passes all four correctly. FIXED — the trace countermeasure now works; nothing remains for Phase 5's R5 on this item."

    my_probes_lied_twice_more: "A boot-wait loop printed 'LISTENING after 1s' because its grep matched before the server was up; verified by reading the log instead (real boot was fine). And a suite-aggregation grep reported verify-tutorial-altpath as blank/failed when it was 11/11 — that harness simply prints no `N/M passed` summary line. Neither was a code defect. CHECK THE PROBE BEFORE BELIEVING THE PROBE, in both directions."
  }

  @shop_and_rig {
    read_first: "SHOP_ARCHITECTURE.md — full read of shop/inventory/equipment/rig (2026-08-31), written before G3 code."

    two_item_universes: "LARGELY HISTORICAL — corrected 2026-09-24. CURRENT FACTS: the in-memory SHOP_CATALOG lives at shopService.ts:110 (not :82) and holds 33 items, not 18 (HARDWARE 9, TOKEN 6, TOOL 4, CONSUMABLE 3, EXPLOIT 3, SOFTWARE 3, DEFENSE 2, UPGRADE 2, MISC 1); the boot sync is index.ts:113 (not :112) and is load-bearing — it is what closed the old P2003 purchase failure. THE SECOND UNIVERSE IS GONE: prisma/seed.ts now holds exactly ONE shopItem reference, a deleteMany() at :426, and writes NO shop rows — the old :2671-2975 block is deleted. HISTORY of the defect: the seeded rows used ids `seed_${name}` — a disjoint id space AND disjoint names (seed 'Port Scanner Pro' vs catalog 'Port Scanner'). Every ACTION (buy/sell/use/equip) resolves via catalog.get; only DISPLAY (getPlayerInventory) falls back to the table. So a seeded item is visible in `scripts` and rejected by every verb. fromDbRow maps unknown categories to MISC, and MISC is not equipable, so all 29 seeded rows are unequipable even if resolved."

    g3_five_broken_links: "PLAN.md scoped G3 as 'all 8 initComputerSpec call sites omit equippedItemNames'. TRUE, and it is the LAST of five links, all broken: (1) the 9 HARDWARE_BONUSES items are not purchasable (seed-only, shop lists the catalog); (2) they cannot be equipped (category 'hardware' -> MISC); (3) ONE slot per category, so at most one hardware item could ever apply — 'more resources' unreachable by design; (4) equippedItemNames never passed; (5) no readout — free/top show a hardcoded level-1 rig. Fixing only (4) would have been a no-op reported as done."

    design_decisions: "D1 hardware is INSTALLED not equipped — leaves the equip system, cumulative across CPU/RAM/BW. Because hardware is non-consumable with maxStack 1 and purchaseItem already rejects a second copy, OWNERSHIP IS INSTALLATION: no new column, no migration, selling uninstalls. D2 SHOP_CATALOG is the only source of truth; the seeded shopItems block is deleted. OPEN: supersede-with-50%-trade-in (recommended, matches the chosen preview) vs stack-all-owned."

    effects_are_decorative: "Two functions sum bonuses by DIFFERENT rules over DIFFERENT sets and neither reaches gameplay: shopService.getPlayerBonuses (whole inventory, IGNORES isEquipped) renders `scripts`; inventoryService.getEquipmentBonuses (equipped only) renders `equipment`. The two panels can disagree. All 7 ItemEffects fields are display-only; cryptographyBonus/networkingBonus columns are written as literal 0 by the sync and never read. useItem decrements and emits under the comment 'this would integrate with other systems'. CORRECTED 2026-09-24 — there are now TWO working item effects, not one: effect.type='persona_message' via tokenConsumption.ts, AND the 9 HARDWARE items, which materially change CPU/RAM/BW through resolveInstalledHardware (gameBalance.ts:115-123) feeding memoryService.initComputerSpec (:214-216). Equipping is cosmetic — the sole real coupling is OWNERSHIP gating hack tool bonuses (hackCommands.ts:849 -> hasItem -> hackService's own hardcoded TOOL_EFFECTIVENESS table). Zero listeners on all 7 shop/inventory events."

    memory_service_lifecycle_dead: "initializeSession (memoryService.ts:674) and cleanupSession (:683) have ZERO callers. Consequences: registerTerminal never runs so the terminal passive consumer does not exist; baseSpecs.delete appears only inside the dead cleanupSession so all four per-user maps LEAK for the server lifetime and survive reconnects; registerActiveTrace has a caller (hackService.ts:2032) and — CORRECTED 2026-09-24 — unregisterActiveTrace NOW HAS ONE TOO (traceService.ts:550, via _releaseTraceDrain, on both evade and completion), so the trace's 15 CPU/16 RAM drain is no longer permanent. Also registerConnection/registerBackdoor/unregister* — all zero callers."

    resource_display_lies: "HEAD IS STALE — corrected 2026-09-24: initComputerSpec IS now reached from command handling, via refreshComputerSpec (commandModules/helpers.ts:164-180), invoked from 9 sites (processCommands.ts:102, networkCommands.ts:1276, helpers.ts:204, hackCommands.ts:394/1015/1391/1476/1560/1978). HISTORY: no handler called it, getComputerSpec fell back to calculateBaseSpec(1), and a level-40 player who typed `free`/`top` saw a hardcoded 200/256/100 until their first process spawn. The client store defaults to the same numbers. resources:update skips players with no running processes (`if (userProcesses.size === 0) continue`) so idle bars sit stale. Bandwidth is never rendered client-side at all. G3 must fix this or the feature is invisible and untestable by the player."

    client_intercepts_commands: "Terminal.svelte:726-746 intercepts shop/inventory/equipment/gear/scripts into GUI dialogs BEFORE they reach the server, dispatching on cmdParts[0] and DISCARDING the arguments. So `shop EXPLOIT` — the server's own help example — cannot reach the server from a browser, and the server's ASCII multiPanel boxes are unreachable in the web client. buy/sell/use/equip/unequip are not intercepted."

    top_defects: "S1 crack.protected is unusable by anyone — matcher looks for 'quantum charge', item is 'Quantum Decryptor Charge' (VERIFIED BY RUNNING the substring test = false); player is told 'Requires a Quantum Decryptor Charge' while holding one, and `use quantum_charge` destroys the 7500c item for nothing. S5 EVERY example item id in the shop help is fictional (port_scanner/firewall/health_pack/stealth_module — none of the 18 real ids), so `man buy` teaches a failing command. S15 darknet rare_script reward never grants ('zero_day_exploit' vs row named 'Zero-Day Exploit'). S12 no @@unique([userId,shopItemId]) + every reader uses findFirst = duplicates under-report silently. S13 architectInterventionExecutor does an unconditional create with an UNVALIDATED AI-supplied shopItemId (reopens P2003). S14 mission credits use absolute assignment from a stale read instead of increment, losing concurrent grants. S20 reseed hazard: seed.ts:425 shopItem.deleteMany() with no onDelete on the FK defaults to Restrict, so reseeding a DB where anyone owns an item throws."

    tier1_string_bugs: "DONE 2026-08-31 (S1/S5/S15), verified against a live DB. S1 crack.protected now resolves the charge BY CATALOG ID (new QUANTUM_CHARGE_ITEM_ID in gameBalance.ts, following the HACK_TOOL_ITEMS id convention) with a scoped findFirst instead of pulling the whole inventory and filtering in JS. S5 all shop help example ids replaced with real catalog ids; `shop`'s [search] arg REMOVED from the help rather than left advertised, because S7 makes it return unbuyable items. S15 darknet reward field renamed scriptName->scriptItemId and looked up by id; legacy scriptName on persisted rewardData is still read so no data migration needed; a missing row now WARNS (the silence is why it paid nothing for as long as it existed). RUNTIME PROOF: shopItem.findFirst({name:'zero_day_exploit'}) returns NULL on the live DB while findUnique({id:'zero_day_exploit'}) returns the row named 'Zero-Day Exploit'."

    verify_shop_contract: "scripts/verify-shop-contract.ts (5/5) closes the BUG CLASS, not the 3 instances: checks help example ids, HACK_TOOL_ITEMS, QUANTUM_CHARGE_ITEM_ID, darknet reward ids, and BANS matching items by name substring. Every check was NEGATIVE-TESTED — each bug reintroduced and the FAIL confirmed, then reverted. Throws rather than passing vacuously if the catalog parse yields 0 ids, 0 example ids are checked, or 0 darknet rewards are found (the exact failure mode that let verify-mission-provisioning pass with 0 switch arms)."

    D2_CORRECTION: "'Delete the seeded shopItems block' would BREAK THE ONLY WORKING ITEM EFFECT IN THE GAME. 6 of the 19 seeded rows are itemType:'token' persona tokens (Commander Steele's Briefing Token, gh0st's Dead Drop Token, Director Chen's Business Card, AIDA Signal Fragment, Envoy's Cipher Token, Architect's Seal) and they are LIVE: tokenConsumption.ts gates persona messaging on them, missionService drops them as rewards, darknet aida_token grants one. They must MOVE INTO SHOP_CATALOG, not be deleted. Live DB: 37 ShopItem rows = 18 catalog + 19 seeded."

    g3_done: "DONE 2026-08-31. scripts/verify-g3-hardware.ts 19/19 over the REAL SOCKET PATH asserting NUMBERS. 9 hardware + 6 persona tokens MOVED into SHOP_CATALOG (4 software duplicates dropped); new ItemCategory.HARDWARE (deliberately NOT in equipableCategories, so equip refuses it) and ItemCategory.TOKEN (lowercased -> itemType 'token', which missionService/darknetDungeonService query on). HARDWARE_SPECS in gameBalance.ts maps catalog id -> {channel, amount, tier}; resolveInstalledHardware keeps only the HIGHEST TIER PER CHANNEL. Supersession trades the old part in at 50% INSIDE THE PURCHASE TRANSACTION (a follow-up step would charge for the upgrade and pay no refund on a crash between the two). One refreshComputerSpec helper in helpers.ts replaces the level-only call at all 9 sites. New `specs` command + ALL process readouts refresh the rig first (closes S10 — without it every purchase still looks inert). reconcileShopItems runs at BOOT as well as seed, because existing DBs hold seed_* rows and are never reseeded. MEASURED on a level-30 player (baseline 500/640/250): RAM 640->704 on tier 1, then 768 on tier 2 NOT 832, 'Traded in RAM Module Mk1 (+250 credits)', net spend 1750."

    g3_harness_caught_two: "The harness FAILED 13/19 on its first run and both causes were real. (1) Four orphaned seed_* rows survived — the reconcile only deleted ids in its rename map, so the software duplicates (moved nowhere, catalog equivalents exist) were stranded; it now sweeps EVERY unreferenced seed_* row and SKIPS WITH A WARNING any row a player still holds, because InventoryItem.shopItemId has no onDelete and defaults to Restrict. (2) MY OWN harness bug: the test player was level 1, so `buy ram_module_mk2` was CORRECTLY refused (tier 2 needs level 10) and 4 assertions failed for a reason unrelated to supersession — fixed by levelling to 30, which is also why every assertion is a DELTA from a measured baseline rather than an absolute, since level feeds the same numbers."

    purchasable_flag: "CORRECTED 2026-09-24 — `purchasable` is NOT a Prisma column. It is a TS interface field on the catalog type (shopService.ts:27), persisted as `isActive: item.purchasable !== false` (:705); the DB column is ShopItem.isActive. It is false for reward-only items. All 6 persona tokens carried isActive:false in the seed, so moving them into the catalog without this would have put a 5000-credit 'message Commander Steele' button in the shop. Every BROWSE path filters via sellableItems(); every RESOLVE path (getItem/use/sell/inventory) does not, so a granted token stays usable. purchaseItem checks it as the actual boundary, since buy takes an arbitrary id from the player. ALSO: syncCatalogToDatabase did NOT write the `effect` column at all before G3 — it had to learn to, or the move would have silently broken tokenConsumption, the only working item effect in the game."

    S20_WAS_WRONG: "I claimed reseeding would throw on the ShopItem FK because InventoryItem has no onDelete. It would NOT: seed.ts deletes inventoryItem BEFORE shopItem, so the order is already safe. The other half (upsert with update:{} never refreshing existing rows) was real and is now moot — the seed no longer writes shop items at all. Verify claims about deletion ORDER by reading the order, not by reasoning from the constraint."

    balance_notes: "Math.floor(level/10) means levels 1-9 give IDENTICAL resources — no growth across most of the early game. `nice` is half-wired: only hack/exploit read the stored priority, so it silently does nothing for scan/probe/download/decrypt/analyze/sweep/whois/traceroute."
  }

  @soft_gate_coverage {
    read_first: "PLAN.md U3c section — coverage audit 2026-08-31."

    U3c_0_FIXED: "FIXED 2026-08-31, closing Phase 1. processHackAttempt now takes skillPenaltySeverity and forwards it to calculateHackParameters (which ALREADY supported it — only the parameter was missing). All SIX call sites thread it: process path AND no-resource fallback for exploit/backdoor/rootkit, since the fallback would otherwise be a free attempt whenever memoryService is absent. `crack` takes its penalty as a HARDER CHALLENGE instead — brute-force difficulty += severity * SKILL_PENALTY.maxMinigameDifficultyBump (new, 3 points on a 1-10 scale) — the first piece of decision 12 to ship. TWO SILENT NO-OPS FIXED ALONGSIDE: `crack` selected cryptography and `backdoor` selected only stealth, but ALL FIVE soft commands gate on `hacking`, so getSkillShortfall would have read a missing field and returned severity 0 — a penalty that never bites. Always cross-check the handler's `select` against the skill the REQUIREMENT names."

    submit_softlock_FIXED: "FIXED 2026-08-31. crack.dict/mask/pattern are now 'unblockable'. They gate on Cryptography 20/25/20 but answer a session opened by `crack`, which gates on HACKING 30 — a player could open a file-crack session and then be refused permission to answer it, unwinnable and not abandonable into progress. sweep.reveal made unblockable too: it was safe ONLY because its gate coincidentally equalled sweep's (Forensics 15 both), which stops being true the moment sweep goes soft. RULE: any command that ANSWERS a challenge the game already started belongs in the unblockable set — its difficulty was set from the player's skill at GENERATION time, so a second check at answer time only strands them."

    REGRESSION_U3c_0_CLOSED: "CLOSED — verified 2026-09-24, retire this entry. getSkillShortfall now has NINE call sites, not two, and processHackAttempt DOES take a severity parameter (hackService.ts:293), so crack/exploit/backdoor/rootkit are penalised as designed. HISTORY: they were declared mode:'soft' with NO PENALTY WIRED for any of them. So U3 shipped a STRICTLY EASIER GAME for those four: attemptable 15 points below requirement at zero cost. Violates the doctrine in skillRequirements.ts:41-50, which I wrote in the same change. The penalty was wired; no action remains on this item."

    design_decision_12: "Maintainer's model supersedes decision 9's 'penalty currency' framing: an under-skilled attempt should be HARDER (minigame difficulty scales with shortfall), RISKIER (external consequence — discovery/trace/owner alerted, not just a worse result), and REWARDED when cleared anyway. Prerequisite: the skill needs a minigame, a process time, and a resource cost to hang these on."

    coverage_matrix: "ONLY TWO commands have all three prerequisites: `sweep` (anomaly_scan/disk_sector minigame + sweep process 60/64/20) and `hack` (layered minigame + hack_prep 80/128/50). PROCESS BUT NO MINIGAME (9): decrypt, analyze, probe, traceroute, scan, trace.evade, exploit, backdoor, rootkit. INSTANT+FREE+CONSEQUENCE-FREE (13): encrypt, decode, subnet, protect, safevault, honeypot, security.scan, backdoor.remove, key.contact, collar.shield, share_intel, proxy, alias:reveal. So decision 12 is buildable TODAY only for sweep and hack; everything else needs a minigame/process/resource invented first = Phase 8/9 FEATURE WORK, not a Phase 1 gate fix."

    minigame_difficulty_barely_responds: "calculateLayerDifficulty = securityLevel + layerIndex*0.5 - relevantSkill/25 + methodModifier. Lower skill DOES make it harder, but the coefficient is tiny: a full 15-point shortfall (the entire soft band) moves difficulty by 0.6 on a 1-10 scale. And generateLayersForServer(serverProfile, skills, method) takes NO severity argument, so the soft-gate shortfall never reaches it. crack.storm is worse — difficulty hard-coded to 10 (hackCommands.ts:1218), ignoring both file encryptionLevel and player skill."

    soft_lock_class_again_WAS_WRONG: "RETIRED AS STALE 2026-09-24. This entry claimed crack.dict/crack.mask/crack.pattern are mode 'hard'. They are mode:'unblockable' (skillRequirements.ts:104-106) — exactly what submit_softlock_FIXED, two entries above in this same section, already records. It was a stale duplicate of an already-closed item and it contradicted its own neighbour. Kept only as an example of prose drifting against prose."

    adjacent_defects_filed: "alias:reveal is DEAD — aliasService.ts:198-200 reads skills from the progress.skills JSON column (line drifted from :194; RE-VERIFIED STILL LIVE 2026-09-24 against schema.prisma:159 and the threshold of 40 at aliasService.ts:202 — `alias reveal` is mathematically unable to succeed), but skills are top-level Int columns and that JSON defaults to {}, so combinedSkill is always 0 vs a threshold of 40 (Phase 5). backdoor.use PRINTS 'The server owner has been alerted' but no alert fires — backdoor:discovered is emitted on the service's own EventEmitter with no subscriber (Phase 5). sweep spawns its process BEFORE checking any hidden files exist, burning resources on a guaranteed no-op (Phase 5)."
  }

  @hacking {
    HackService: "Two flows: processHackAttempt (RNG) + initiateHackSession (3-layer interactive minigame). DB session persistence. Home defense: firewall prepended, vault appended, IDS alerts. NUMBERS CORRECTED 2026-09-24 — 'stealth -8%', '5% floor' and 'cancel: 20% partial detection + 15s cooldown' were ALL WRONG. Real behaviour: the priority detectionModifier is CLAMPED to [-0.20, +0.30] (memoryService.ts:153), and abortSession adds detectionAccumulator += 10 and applies NO cooldown at all (hackService.ts:868-870)."
    BackdoorService: "Real method names (corrected 2026-09-24, the old list was paraphrase): installBackdoor, useBackdoor, scanForBackdoors, removeBackdoor, plus removeDetectedBackdoor, getBackdoors, cleanupExpired. Types: standard, persistent, rootkit(permanent) — and the 24h/72h figures are BASE hours only, scaled by the installer's stealth and capped by BACKDOOR_DURATION_MAX_* (gameBalance.ts:168-181). Detection risk increases per use."
    TraceService: "Real method names (corrected 2026-09-24): initiateTrace, progressTraces, evadeTrace — not initiate/progress/evade. 60s auto-tick; evade is a stealth check. Duration tiers: 15m/30m/1h/2h by evidence."

    @detection_consequences {
      low_0_30: "Silent logging only"
      medium_31_60: "Firewall +1 (30min), owner notified"
      high_61_80: "Firewall +2, security +1 (1hr), faction AI alerted (FactionKnowledge + PersonaService), rep -5, owner notified"
      critical_81_100: "Full lockdown (fw max 2hr), trace initiated (passive drain), key revoked, faction alerted, rep -15, BOUNTY POSTED"
      faction_reaction: "Leader learns attacker via FactionKnowledge → counter-missions"
    }

    @bounty_system {
      model: "Bounty — targetUserId, targetUsername, issuedByFactionId, reason, rewardCredits/Rep, status, claimedByUserId, stolenFileIds (Json), expiresAt (48h)"
      creation: "Critical evidence (81%+) → postBounty() finds downloaded files, records IDs, creates bounty, notifies faction, AI leader posts wanted notice"
      reward_scaling: "Base 1000c + (evidence-80)*200c. 5 + (evidence-80) rep."
      commands: "'bounties' lists active (16-char id prefix). 'bounty claim <id|prefix>' accepts. 'bounty complete <id>' verifies hack + deletes stolen files + revokes keys + grants rewards. Logic lives in services/bountyService.ts (2026-10-07); before that the displayed prefix could not be claimed at all, so this loop had NEVER run (dev DB: zero bounties ever)."
      invariants_2026_10_07: "claim = atomic updateMany {status active, unclaimed, unexpired, not self}. complete = transition claimed->completed + addCredits in ONE transaction; only the winner pays rep/purges/notifies. Proof = a serverConnection with accessLevel>0 on the target home whose connectedAt >= bounty.createdAt (rows are never pruned). Nothing writes status 'expired' — every 'live' query must also filter expiresAt > now. decoysHit is always 0 (decoys have sourceServerId 'decoy'; stolen files are matched by the breached server id) — open question."
      pvp_loop: "Detection → bounty → faction notified → hunter claims → hacks target home → stolen files deleted + keys revoked → reward. Creates organic PvP."
    }

    @download_system {
      command: "'download <file>' — reads source, spawns process, copies to ~/downloads/"
      access_keys: "Detection ONLY on download. Keys linked to file via sourceFileId."
      metadata: "FileSystemNode.metadata: { sourceServerId, sourcePath, downloadedAt, isDownloaded }. Used by bounty system."
      key_revocation: "deleteNode() auto-revokes ServerAccessKeys with matching sourceFileId + triggers honeypot alert if decoy."
      gameplay_loop: "Explore (cat) → find valuable file → download → keys extracted → access new servers. Caught → bounty → hunter deletes downloads → lose keys. Must re-steal."
    }

    @home_defense_system {
      schema: "PlayerProgress: homeFirewall(0-3), homeVault(0-3), homeIds(0-3), homeHoneypot(Boolean)"
      commands: "defenses, protect <dir>, safevault [status|move|retrieve], honeypot [status|refresh], upgrade <defense> [level]"
      skill_gates: "defenses/upgrade ungated. protect→Networking 15. safevault→Crypto 20. honeypot→Stealth 25."

      @firewall {
        levels: "L1: 2000c, L2: 5000c, L3: 12000c"
        effect: "Adds port_sequence layers PREPENDED. L1→diff 5, L2→diff 7, L3→diff 9 + cipher."
      }

      @vault {
        levels: "L1: 3000c, L2: 8000c, L3: 20000c"
        effect: "Hidden ~/.vault/ dir. Files inside isProtected + isHidden."
        minigame: "Vault layers APPENDED. L1→cipher(6). L2→cipher+memory_trace(8). L3→cipher+memory_trace+port_sequence(9)."
        commands: "'safevault move/retrieve <file>'"
      }

      @ids {
        levels: "L1: 1500c, L2: 4000c, L3: 10000c"
        effect: "IDS alerts via Socket.IO"
        timing: "L1→alert on completion. L2→alert on start. L3→start + attacker IP/username on completion."
      }

      @honeypot {
        price: "5000c one-time"
        effect: "3-5 decoy files in ~/downloads/ (metadata.isDecoy). Reading triggers alert with attacker identity."
        commands: "'honeypot refresh' regenerates decoys."
      }

      @folder_protection {
        command: "'protect <dir>' toggles isProtected"
        effect: "Protected files can't be deleted/moved/modified by attackers. Hidden from low-access intruders."
      }
    }
  }

  @factions {
    FactionService: "CRUD, join/leave (standing checks), addReputation (clamping + cross-faction rivalry), ranks (recruit→operative→elite→council_member). 4 canonical: garrison, dothackers, cybercorp, darknet."
    ReputationEngine: "Rivalry matrix: garrison↔dothackers(-0.5), dothackers↔cybercorp(-0.6), garrison+cybercorp(+0.2), darknet vs all(-0.3). Thresholds: ≥30 allied, ≤-30 hostile."
    ResourceService: "5-min tick resource gen from faction servers. Types: credits, intel, compute."
    ContestService: "Territory contests. Real method names (corrected 2026-09-24): declareContest, joinContest, contribute, resolveContest. Layer-based challenge."
    WarfareService: "Faction wars: declare (AI-only), surrender, score, 2x rep multiplier, resource bleed, 14-day ceasefire."
    AliasService: "Identity aliases: create (10k), destroy, attemptReveal (skill check — the method is attemptReveal, not reveal; corrected 2026-09-24). 3x replacement limit. NOTE: the reveal path is DEAD — see adjacent_defects_filed under @soft_gate_coverage."
    DarkNetDiscoveryService: "4 discovery paths: hidden_file (.aida), skill_threshold (hacking≥60+stealth≥50), censorship_flags (3+), breadcrumb_trail (3+ encrypted). AIDA sends AI recruitment DM."

    @share_intel_gating {
      skill_gate: "socialEng ≥ 10 via SKILL_REQUIREMENTS"
      rank_gate: "Must be operative+ — checked in gameCommands.handleShareIntel()"
    }
    CensorshipService: "Regex filtering on forum/messages/cat. Alerts trigger DarkNet discovery check."
  }

  @ai {
    AIService: "Ollama REST /api/chat. Model: the default in code is 'llama3.1:8b' (aiService.ts:90), not nemotron-3-super:cloud — corrected 2026-09-24. generateResponse() returns {success, response, error}. Timeout is a FLAT 120000ms for all modes (:98), not 60s/120s. 3 retries with 429-aware backoff. Concurrency throttle (max 2 parallel). Retry queue: 30s interval, max 20, 3 attempts, 10min TTL. Agent loop (aiAgentTools.ts): 28 tools (recounted 2026-09-24 by three independent audit slices; the old '24 tools (19 query + 5 creation)' was wrong), max 6 rounds per request."
    PersonaService: "AI NPC facade + event handlers. 4 faction leaders + Game Master. Event handlers for join/leave/rank/contest/mission/hack/war/forum. Smart fallbacks: faction-voiced templates when AI is down (welcome, departure, promotion messages). All AI failures queued for retry. Delegates mission gen to PersonaMissionGenService, decisions to PersonaActionService."
    PersonaMissionGenService: "Template-driven mission generation. generateDynamicMission() 10-step pipeline: template selection → knowledge-aware objective filling → reward scaling → AI flavor text. Used by PersonaService + PersonaActionService."
    PersonaActionService: "AI decision pipeline. buildNarrativeContext() → decideDirectorAction() (GM) / decideAction() (leaders) → executeAction(). SIX action types, not five (corrected 2026-09-24): issue_mission, create_story_arc, send_message, forum_post, trigger_event, and plant_discovery (personaActionService.ts:747)."
    AISchedulerService: "4hr faction leaders, 8hr others. 3 actions/day limit. Midnight reset + knowledge verification. 30-min state check: low resources → defensive, contested → defensive, war → war-support, imbalance → rebalancing. Calls expireEntries() + decayConfidence() + purgeOldEntries()."
    StoryProgressionService: "Architect Staging Engine. Records events → evaluates via AI (≥5 unprocessed) → synthesizes world state → manages epochs. 4 pillars: RECORD → EVALUATE → SYNTHESIZE → EPOCH. Reactive Architect: weight ≥ 8 events trigger immediate mini-evaluation (10min cooldown, single intervention)."
    ArchitectInterventionExecutor: "7 types: send_message, plant_clue, trigger_event, adjust_tension, create_mission, grant_token, reveal_faction. executeBatch() + StoryLedger recording. checkInterventionOutcomes() tracks clue discovery, mission engagement, message replies — included in Architect evaluation prompt."
    DarkNetDungeonService: "Procedural chains of 4-8 servers (depth 3-7, servers = depth+1; corrected 2026-09-24). Encrypted breadcrumbs. AI forum riddles. conquerVault() grants rewards, records to StoryLedger, auto-regenerates 30s. 7-day TTL."
  }

  @social {
    MessageService: "Core messaging: send/receive/inbox/sent/read/delete. Delivery queue with 5s processor. Token-gated AI persona messaging (sendTokenMessage + generatePersonaReply). Post-send hook for tutorial. Delegates encryption to MessageEncryptionService. Emits message:received/new_mail/read_receipt."
    MessageEncryptionService: "AES-256-CBC encryption/decryption. encryptMessage(), decryptMessage(), decryptMessageById(), crackEncryption() (gameplay mechanic with XP). Pure crypto, no Socket.IO."
    ChatService: "Chat-specific operations: getChatHistory(), getChatContacts(), markConversationRead(), getUnreadChatCounts(). Emits message:conversation_read."
    ForumService: "Enhanced (Phase 3A+4). Posts with censorship filtering. Replies, votes, reports. Emits forum:post_created."
    PlayerPresenceService: "Online status via Socket.IO connect/disconnect."
  }

  @supporting {
    ShopService: "Catalog + inventory CRUD via InventoryItem table. purchaseItem() atomic $transaction. getPlayerInventory(), addItemToInventory(), removeItemFromInventory(), sellItem() all use InventoryItem table (no JSON fields)."
    InventoryService: "Equipment management via InventoryItem.isEquipped + slot fields. equipItem(), unequipItem(), getEquipment(), getEquipmentBonuses() all query InventoryItem table. No JSON fields."
    MemoryService: "CPU/RAM/BW management. GameProcess lifecycle, passive consumers, 1s tick, Socket.IO push. Hardware items boost specs."
    ProcessStateService: "Command execution tracking with cleanup timers."
    LeaderboardService: "DB-backed, 9 categories. getLeaderboard() + getPlayerRank(). ASCII table."
    AchievementService: "28 achievements, 7 categories. checkAndAward() auto-checks, emits achievement:unlocked. Hooked to mission:completed + hack:attempt."
  }
}

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CLIENT / UI
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@client {
  description: "Svelte 5 terminal-first UI using Svelte 4 legacy patterns (export let, createEventDispatcher, onMount — NOT runes). Commands → server → ASCII text back. Reactive overlays for real-time data."
  directory: "client/"
  architecture: "Terminal.svelte (main, ~1955 lines) + dialog components + notification panel. ForumDialog = 'forum terminal' with keyboard shortcuts (R/N/V/S/J/T/!/M/:)."

  @components {
    Terminal: "1955 lines — full-screen terminal, CRT effects, status bar (CPU/RAM gauges, notifications, clock), tab completion + history, hack challenge panel, keyboard shortcuts (Ctrl+T/W/L, Ctrl+1-9). Responsive (1024/768/480px + reduced-motion + high contrast)."
    TerminalTabs: "Multi-terminal tabs. VS Code style, per-tab output/history."
    AuthDialog: "Login/Register modal with validation."
    AsciiDialog: "Reusable ASCII-bordered dialog (╔═╗). Focus trap, Escape close, scanline overlay."
    ChatDialog: "Real-time chat. Contact sidebar with avatars, online status, unread badges. Message grouping (5-min). Encryption toggle (🔒/🔓 → --encrypt). Typing indicators. Keyboard nav."
    ForumDialog: "Keyboard-driven forum (R/N/V/S/J/!/T/:/M/F). Breadcrumb nav. All logic server-side."
    MailDialog: "Inbox/Sent. Category tabs (ALL/PRIV/SYS/MISSION/FACTION/ALERT) with unread counts. Avatars. Decrypt button. Real-time via newMailNotifications store. Encryption on compose. N/R/D/Tab/Enter/Esc."
    ShopDialog: "Category filtering, search, item detail, purchase validation."
    EquipmentDialog: "Inventory grid + Equipment slots (TOOL/SOFTWARE/EXPLOIT/DEFENSE/UPGRADE). Bonuses."
    NotificationPanel: "6 types, max 50. Sound + Desktop API."
  }

  @services {
    api_ts: "REST client (singleton). Auth via httpOnly cookie (credentials:'include') + in-memory token for Socket.IO. Legacy localStorage tokens auto-migrated on first load. CSRF fetched on load after verify; auto-retry on 403; failed → logout. Sections: auth, users, servers, files, messages, forum, missions, hacking, events, commands, health."
    socket_ts: "Socket.IO client (singleton). Stores: socketConnected, socketError, onlineUsers, serverActivity, liveMessages, hackAttempts, playerResources, activeProcesses, activeHackSession, typingUsers, newMailNotifications. Emitters: typing start/stop. Lazy-loads NotificationService. RECONNECTION: socket.io's built-in reconnection is DISABLED (reconnection:false) because it raced the hand-rolled handleReconnect() loop. That loop is therefore the ONLY retry path, and it retries INDEFINITELY with exponential backoff capped at 30s (maxReconnectDelay) — it must not grow an attempt ceiling, because socket.io's default was reconnectionAttempts:Infinity and a 5-attempt cap is only ~31 seconds, which made any laptop sleep or server restart a permanent disconnect. It re-arms even when connect() no-ops. (2026-09-24)"
    terminal_ts: "POST /api/command/execute. Normalizes output to string[]. Error extraction with HTTP status mapping."
    terminalTabs_ts: "Multi-tab state via socket events. Per-tab output + history."
    notifications_ts: "NotificationService + stores. Desktop Notification API + Web Audio (800Hz sine beep)."
  }

  @stores {
    file: "client/src/stores/gameState.ts"
    writable: ["outputLines (max 1000 lines)" "commandHistory" "historyIndex" "currentUser" "isAuthenticated" "authLoading" "authError" "networkAccess" "currentServer" "currentDirectory" "playerProgress" "discoveryLevel" "knownServers" "connectedServers" "fileSystemCache" "onlinePlayerCount" "recentActivity" "unreadMessages" "securityAlerts"]
    derived: ["connectionStatus (socketConnected + authLoading)" "terminalPrompt (user/server/directory)"]
    functions: "addOutput, addSystemOutput, addErrorOutput, addSuccessOutput, clearOutput, addToHistory, navigateHistory, registerUser, loginUser, logoutUser, verifyAuthentication, loadInitialGameData, connectToServer, disconnectFromServer, loadServerFileSystem, sendMessage, attemptHack, initializeGameState"
  }

  @client_utils {
    forumSystem_ts: "Minimal UI-only state (logic server-side). Stores: currentForum, discoveredForums, currentPost."
    note: "asciiAvatars.ts and messagingSystem.ts DELETED — avatars server-generated, MessageDialog removed."
    note_lore: "World lore server-side only (server/src/lore/worldLore.ts)"
  }

  @socket_events {
    notification_wired: "process:completed/failed, mission:objective:updated/completed/expired, player:levelup, faction:event, discovery:made, notification, game:event, forum:new-post/reply, achievement:unlocked, story:key-fragment, story:fragment-stolen, story:fragment-transferred, story:endgame-unlocked, story:endgame-completed"
    store_wired: "process:started/completed/cancelled/progress → activeProcesses. resources:update → playerResources. command:result session → activeHackSession. typing → typingUsers. message:new_mail → newMailNotifications."
    silent: "rewards:xp_granted, rewards:credits_granted — in command output, no popup"
  }

  @status_bar {
    description: "Real CPU/RAM % from playerResources store (5s update via resources:update Socket.IO)."
  }

  @hack_challenge_panel {
    description: "Sticky above input. Visible when activeHackSession.active=true. Shows target IP, layer progress, challenge, hints. Player types crack.submit/firewall.knock/memory.extract."
  }

  @notification_panel {
    description: "6 types, max 50. Sound on high/critical. Desktop Notification API. Ctrl+N toggle. PRIORITY VOCABULARY IS low|normal|high|critical (notifications.ts:18) — the client used to say 'urgent', which the SERVER NEVER SENDS, so those notifications matched no sound, no colour, and no CSS rule. Renamed 2026-09-24; the .notif-priority CSS rule is interpolated from the raw priority value, so a rename must cover the stylesheet too."
  }
}

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SHARED TYPES
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@shared {
  file: "shared/types/ — 11 domain files + index.ts barrel, 1026 lines, 104 unique exports: auth(76) error(41) event(58) faction(103) filesystem(93) game(211) hack(134) mission(110) network(110) npc(37) socket(41). NOTE: shared/types.ts NO LONGER EXISTS. A second tracked subtree shared/shell/ (lexer, parser, args, index) is undocumented here."
  compiled: "shared/types.js + shared/types.d.ts + source maps"
  path_alias: "Server tsconfig: @/shared/* → ../shared/*"

  @categories [
    "Auth: UserRole, User, AuthRequest, AuthResponse, ApiResponse, AvatarInfo"
    "Session: PlayerSession, TerminalTab, Command, ParsedCommand, CommandResult, ValidationResult"
    "Server: ServerState, GameState, CurrentServerInfo, GameServerInfo, ServerConnectionInfo"
    "Player: PlayerInfo, PlayerSkills, PlayerStats, PlayerAliasInfo"
    "Faction: FactionId, FactionRank, FactionReputation, FactionResources, FactionStandingInfo, FactionServerInfo, FactionWarInfo, WarStatus"
    "Network: IPRange, IPZone, IPOwner, DiscoveryResult, TraceRouteHop/Result, ServerDiscoveryResult, ServerScanOptions"
    "Hacking: HackAttempt, HackMethod, HackResult, HackCalculation, HackDifficultyFactors, HackSessionInfo, MinigameType, MinigameChallenge, LayerResult"
    "FileSystem: FileSystemNode, PermissionLevel (bitmask), SpecialAccess, FilePermissions, FileOperation/Type, FileAccessRecord/Summary"
    "Missions: MissionInfo, MissionStatus, MissionObjective, MissionObjectiveMetadata, MissionReward, MissionProgress, ObjectiveProgress, MissionObjectiveType (30+ types)"
    "Events: GameEvent, EventType (17), EventSeverity, EventSubscription, SubscriptionMethod"
    "Notifications: Notification, NotificationType, NotificationPriority"
    "Socket: SocketEventData, StateUpdateEvent, StateDelta, CommandExecuteEvent, BroadcastMessage/Target"
    "Home: PlayerHomeSystem, HomeCustomization"
    "Save: SaveTrigger, SavePriority, ProgressBackup"
    "Errors: GameError, ValidationError, AuthorizationError, NotFoundError, RateLimitError"
    "NPC: NPCAgent, NPCType, NPCState, NPCPersonality"
    "DarkNet: DarkNetDiscoveryMethod, CensorshipAlert"
    "Inventory: InventoryItem"
    "Contest: ServerContestInfo, ContestStatus"
  ]
}

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DATABASE SCHEMA
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@database_schema {
  models: 70
  file: "server/prisma/schema.prisma"

  @source_of_truth [
    "schema.prisma IS the source of truth. It is declarative and tracked in git."
    "prisma/migrations/ is a DERIVED ARTIFACT, not the authority — 0001_init was generated FROM schema.prisma. If the directory is lost it is reproducible in one command; see @migrations."
    "THIS SECTION is a navigational summary, not the authority. It must be updated whenever a model is added or a field's meaning changes — it drifted to 'models: 61' while the schema had 66, and listed User.role without 'npc' after npc became a real role."
  ]

  @core {
    User: "id, username (unique), email (unique), password, homeIp (unique), homeServerId, isOnline, role (player|moderator|admin|npc), mutedUntil. NOTE role=npc marks synthetic AI/NPC accounts — it keeps them out of adminApi/stats player counts and marks server-owning NPCs; see @server_ownership and @ai_user_identity."
    UserSession: "JWT tracking (token unique), expiresAt, isActive, ipAddress, userAgent, lastServerId, currentDirectory. NO @@index AT ALL — the only indexes are the implicit PK and the unique on token (schema.prisma:100-115)."
    PlayerProgress: "userId (PK), experience (NOT 'XP'), level, credits, discoveryLevel, skillPoints (unspent — added after its absence was a LIVE bug: darknetDungeonService wrote skillPoints in the same update as experience, Prisma rejected the unknown column, safeExecute swallowed it, and the XP went with it; nothing spends them yet, schema.prisma:126-134), skills (hacking/networking/cryptography/stealth/socialEng/forensics Int), repMilitary/repSwordCorp/repAnons/repNeutral, missionProgress (Json — DEPRECATED, superseded by PlayerMission + PlayerMissionObjective), equipment (Json — DEPRECATED, use InventoryItem.isEquipped), inventory (Json — DEPRECATED, use InventoryItem table), homeFirewall(0-3), homeVault(0-3), homeIds(0-3), homeHoneypot(Bool), achievements(String[])"
    ProgressBackup: "PlayerProgress snapshots. data (Json), reason, checksum. TWO SEPARATE single-column indexes — @@index([userId]) and @@index([createdAt]) — NOT one composite (schema.prisma:190-191)."
    AuditLog: "userId, action, resource, resourceId, old/newValues"
    GameConfig: "key (PK), value (Json)"
    GameEvent: "type, title, severity, isGlobal, affectedUsers[]"
    EventSubscription: "userId, eventType, targetId, method, quality"
    Notification: "userId, type, title, category, priority, isRead, expiresAt"
  }

  @game_world {
    GameServer: "id, name, ipAddress (unique), type, role, networkId, ownerId, factionId, securityLevel(1-10), firewallLevel(1-10), encryptionLevel(0-5), discoveryLevel(0-5), isPublic, accessMethod, accessKey, isPlayerHome, isAidaHomeServer, isOnline, resourceType/Output, isContested"
    FileSystemNode: "id, serverId, parentId (self-ref), name, type (file|dir), content, permissions (Json bitmask), size, isHidden, isEncrypted, isProtected, metadata (Json?), createdBy"
    ServerConnection: "userId, serverId, accessLevel(0-10), workingDirectory, isActive, sessionData"
    ServerAccessKey: "userId, serverId, keyValue, source, sourceDetail, sourceFileId, discoveredAt. @@unique(userId,serverId)"
  }

  @network {
    Network: "id, name (unique), description, factionId, zone, isHidden, metadata"
    ServerLink: "sourceId, targetId, networkId, linkType, bandwidth, latency, isActive, requiredAccess. @@unique(sourceId,targetId)"
    DiscoveredLink: "userId, linkId, discoveredAt, source. @@unique(userId,linkId)"
  }

  @factions {
    Faction: "id, name (unique), shortName (unique), fullName, description, ideology, color, resources (Json), isHidden, rankRequirements, aiPersonaId (unique FK→AIPersona)"
    FactionMember: "userId, factionId, rank (recruit|operative|elite|council_member), reputation, totalReputationEarned (NOT 'totalRepEarned'), joinedAt. @@unique(userId,factionId)"
    FactionStanding: "userId, factionId, reputation, isAllied/Hostile/Neutral. @@unique(userId,factionId)"
    FactionEvent: "eventType (NOT 'type'), title, description, factionId, userId? (null = global), impact (positive|negative|neutral), reputationChange (NOT 'repChange'), resourceChange (Json?), isRead, triggeredAt. THERE IS NO `data` FIELD — the payload is title + description (schema.prisma:1017-1041)."
    FactionKnowledge: "factionId, assetType (server|file|player), assetId, assetMeta, source, confidence(0-1), discoveredBy, expiresAt. @@unique(factionId,assetType,assetId)"
    FactionResourceTick: "factionId, credits, intel, compute, tickedAt"
  }

  @missions {
    Mission: "title, description, type, difficulty(1-10), objectives, reward, status, assignedTo, createdBy, factionId, issuedBy, storyArcId, storyStep, prerequisiteTemplateIds, targetServerId, expiresAt, timeLimit"
    StoryArc: "title, description, factionId, issuedBy, assignedTo, status (active|completed|failed|abandoned), currentStep, totalSteps, steps (Json), narrativeContext, difficulty"
  }

  @ai {
    AIPersona: "type (game_master|faction_leader|aida), name (unique), personality, systemPrompt, model, actionsToday, lastActionAt"
    AIKnowledge: "personaId, source, type, content, confidence, expiresAt"
    AIAction: "personaId, type, status, input, output, triggeredBy"
    AidaClue: "type, serverId, filePath, content, requiredClues[], difficulty, discovered, discoveredBy. No FK relations."
  }

  @story_discovery {
    StoryProgress: "userId (unique), discoveryLevel(0-6), key fragments (swordFragments/keyFragments/collarFragments 0-3), aidaTrustLevel, endgameUnlocked, endgameChoice, gameCompleted"
    IntelligenceReport: "userId, category, title, importance, triggersEvent"
    KeyFragment: "keyType, fragmentNum, name, description, hint, sourceType, sourceId, heldByUserId, heldSince, status (active|bricked). @@unique(keyType,fragmentNum). heldByUserId is NOT an FK — plain String? with @@index([heldByUserId]) only, no @relation and no back-relation on User (schema.prisma:704,715)."
    KeyFragmentDiscovery: "userId, fragmentId (FK), method. @@unique(userId,fragmentId)"
    NarrativeEpoch: "epochNum (unique), title, summary, worldState (Json), triggers, decisions, startedAt/endedAt"
    StoryLedger: "type, category, actorId, actorType (player|persona ONLY — not faction/system/architect), summary, detail?, data (Json), impact (Json), weight(1-10, ≥7=global), epochNum (NOT 'epochId'), isProcessed. THERE IS NO targetId AND NO targetType (schema.prisma:1661-1683)."
    PersonaMessage: "userId, personaId, tokenItemId, direction (\"inbound\"|\"outbound\" — NOT in|out), subject, content, messageId (NOT 'linkedMessageId' — FK-by-convention to the Message record, no @relation)"
    DarkNetInstance: "networkId (unique FK), gatewayIp, passkey, vaultServerId, depth, difficulty, rewardType, rewardData, status (active|conquered|expired|regenerating), conqueredBy, conqueredAt, expiresAt"
  }

  @social {
    Message: "senderId, recipientId, subject, content, isEncrypted, encryptionKey, messageType, triggerEvent"
    Contact: "userId, contactUserId, handle, encryptionLevel. @@unique(userId,contactUserId)"
  }

  @forum_legacy {
    ForumPost: "authorId, title, forumSection, isHoneypot, factionAlignment (legacy)"
    ForumReply: "postId, authorId, content, votes (legacy)"
  }

  @forum_enhanced {
    description: "Phase 3A+4 enhanced (primary)"
    Forum: "name (unique), url (unique), category, securityLevel(1-5), isHoneypot, factionId, requiresProxy"
    Post: "forumId, authorId, authorHandle, title, isEncrypted, isHidden, storyRelevant, keyFragmentId"
    ForumMember: "userId, forumId, handle, reputation. @@unique(userId,forumId)"
    ForumDiscovery: "userId, forumId, method. @@unique(userId,forumId)"
    ProxyConnection: "userId (unique), proxyServer, location, expiresAt"
    PostReply: "postId, authorId, authorHandle, content, votes"
    PostVote: "userId, postId?, replyId?, value. @@unique per"
    PostReport: "reporterId, postId?, replyId?, forumId, reason, status, resolvedBy"
  }

  @territory {
    ServerContest: "serverId, attackingFactionId, defendingFactionId, initiatedBy, status, decryptionProgress, winnerId"
    ContestParticipant: "contestId, userId, factionId?, contribution, side. @@unique(contestId,userId)"
  }

  @shop_inventory {
    ShopItem: "name, description, itemType, category, price, level, stat bonuses, rarity, isConsumable, stock. effect (Json?) for functional items."
    InventoryItem: "userId, shopItemId, quantity, isEquipped, slot, usesRemaining, expiresAt. source + sourceId for provenance. PRIMARY storage for all player items — replaces legacy JSON fields on PlayerProgress. Equipment tracked via isEquipped (bool) + slot (string)."
    note: "PlayerProgress.inventory and .equipment JSON fields are DEPRECATED — all code now uses InventoryItem table. missionProgress JSON is ALSO DEPRECATED — superseded by the PlayerMission + PlayerMissionObjective tables (schema.prisma:1842,1884); the blob was the root cause of D3 (whole-blob read-modify-write, two writers lost each other's work)."
  }

  @pvp {
    HackSession: "id (manual), attackerId, targetOwnerId, targetServerId, method, currentLayer, totalLayers, status, layersData, detectionAccumulator, timestamps (BigInt epoch ms)"
    Backdoor: "installerId, serverId, accessLevel, type (standard|persistent|rootkit), detectionRisk, expiresAt. @@unique(installerId,serverId)"
    ActiveTrace: "targetId, initiatedBy, serverId, progress(0-100), status, evidenceLevel"
    HackLog: "attackerId, targetId, targetServerId, method, tools[], stealthLevel, success, detected, evidenceLeft"
    Bounty: "targetUserId, targetUsername (cached), issuedByFactionId, reason, rewardCredits, rewardReputation, status, claimedByUserId?, completedAt, expiresAt, serverId?, evidenceLevel, stolenFileIds (Json?). HAS FOUR FKs (D10, schema.prisma:1581-1584): target User(Cascade), claimedBy User?(SetNull), faction Faction(Cascade), server GameServer?(SetNull). The 48h TTL is application-level — expiresAt is a bare required DateTime with no default (schema.prisma:1571)."
  }

  @ai_pipeline_and_queues {
    ContentDraft: "AI-created entities awaiting review. id, type (server|file|link|mission|forum_post|network|forum), title, description, payload (Json), source (ai_content|architect|admin|epoch_event), sourceId, status (draft|applied|rejected), reviewNote, reviewedBy/At, appliedAt, resultId. Approving executes the payload and creates the real entity."
    ContentJob: "Persistent queue for server content generation (replaces fire-and-forget). serverId (FK, cascade), priority (1=urgent 5=normal 10=low), status (pending|processing|completed|failed), attempts/maxAttempts, error, requestedBy, options (Json: skipAI/force), completedAt. @@index([status, priority])"
    PendingPersonaMail: "Deferred persona mail — replies are NOT instant, and generation happens when an item comes due so bursts spread over time. personaId?, senderId, recipientId, subject, content? (pre-rendered) OR prompt?+systemPrompt? (generated at delivery), fallback?, kind (reply|notice), status (pending|sent|failed|cancelled), attempts/maxAttempts, deliverAt, sentAt, error. @@index([status, deliverAt]). See @persona_mail."
    EpochEvent: "Timed story beats. epochId (FK), name, description, triggerType, scheduledAt, condition (Json), payload (Json), status, firedAt, result."
  }

  @moderation {
    MessageReport: "Player-reported direct messages. reporterId, messageId, reason, status, resolvedAt/By. Mirrors PostReport for forums."
  }

  @phase5 {
    FactionWar: "attacker/defenderFactionId, declaredBy, status, scores, repMultiplier, terms"
    PlayerAlias: "userId (unique), aliasName (unique), apparentFactionId, cost, revealedBy[]"
    DarkNetDiscovery: "userId (unique), method, metadata"
    CensorshipRule: "factionId?, serverId?, pattern (regex), replacement, alertTarget"
  }

  @knowledge_and_player_missions {
    description: "Four models that were missing from this section entirely. KnowledgeTopic/PlayerKnowledge are the KNOWLEDGE_DESIGN schema — TABLES ONLY, NO CODE. Verified repo-wide 2026-09-24 (fresh db:reset): both models appear ONLY in schema.prisma (the two definitions plus their relation back-references at :92 and :1798). There is NO creator, reader, or writer anywhere in server/src, server/prisma, shared/, or client/src — not a repository, not a service, not the seed. A fresh seed leaves both tables EMPTY. 'Already landed' means the MIGRATION landed; the feature is unimplemented. This is bug shape #4 (dead code that looks live) applied to the schema, and it is the kind of claim that sends someone looking for the bug in a knowledge system that does not exist yet. PlayerMission/PlayerMissionObjective replace the PlayerProgress.missionProgress JSON blob (D3 pass 2)."
    KnowledgeTopic: "schema.prisma:1779. id, slug (unique — e.g. 'entity.aida'), label (shown at level 1 in place of the term), category (entity|classified|contact|location|event), tier (1-5, selects which existing minigame generator gates the reveal), patterns (String[] regex sources), codexEntry (Text?), revealStyle (hex|glitch), createdAt. @@index([tier]) @@index([category])"
    PlayerKnowledge: "schema.prisma:1807. id, userId (FK User Cascade), topicId (FK KnowledgeTopic Cascade), level (1 = category known '[ENTITY]', 2 = fully revealed), source (minigame:<name>|download|story|skill|trade), sourceRef?, discoveredAt. @@unique(userId,topicId) @@index([userId]). ABSENCE OF A ROW IS LEVEL 0 — that is why there is no level-0 value."
    PlayerMission: "schema.prisma:1842. One player's copy of one mission. id, userId (FK User Cascade), missionId (FK Mission Cascade — 78 of 299 live blob entries pointed at deleted Mission rows), status (available|active|completed|failed|expired), startedAt?, completedAt?, expiresAt?, storyArcId?, storyStep?, metadata (Json? — completeMission reads metadata.detectionCount/.hintCount; nothing writes them yet), createdAt, updatedAt. @@unique(userId,missionId) @@index([userId,status]) @@index([status,expiresAt] — the expiry sweep, the thing the JSON blob could not express as a predicate)"
    PlayerMissionObjective: "schema.prisma:1884. id, playerMissionId (FK PlayerMission Cascade), objectiveId (authored id, e.g. 'u1_breach'), type, description?, targetCount?/currentCount, targetFlag?/currentFlag, targetText?/currentText, completed, isBonus (R7 — a bonus objective does not gate completion), metadata (Json? — entity ids for G6 target matching live HERE, not in target), position. @@unique(playerMissionId,objectiveId). target/current are SPLIT BY TYPE rather than Json so currentCount is incrementable in SQL; which pair is in use is decided by which target is non-null, mirroring G1 (semantics from the runtime type of target, never from type)."
  }
}

