# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# MIGRATION HISTORY
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@migrations {
  total: 0
  directory: "(none — deliberately)"

  @decision [
    "DECISION 2026-08-31 (maintainer): DEFER migrations until there is a live database. The project provisions from schema.prisma with `prisma db push`. prisma/migrations/ has been DELETED and the `_prisma_migrations` bookkeeping table dropped, so the database is in a pure db-push state with no phantom history."
    "WHY: schema.prisma is the source of truth and provisions a fresh database in one command, so migrations add nothing yet. A single baseline is just 'create all 66 tables' — the same thing db push does. Migrations earn their keep by evolving a database you CANNOT DROP, and there is no such database while the project is pre-launch."
    "THE REAL RISK IS HALF-ADOPTION, and this repo already proved it: 30 migrations were documented by name while a 1798-line 0001_baseline sat UNAPPLIED and the live schema was maintained with db push. Committed-but-unmaintained migrations are worse than none, because they look authoritative. Hence: no migrations at all until the workflow actually switches."
  ]

  @adopt_when [
    "TRIGGER: the first database whose data cannot be dropped — first real deployment or first real players. Secondary trigger: a second person/machine that must converge on the schema without resetting."
    "Adoption recipe (cheap while there is no data, fiddly after): npx prisma migrate dev --name init  → generates a baseline from schema.prisma and applies it. For an existing populated database instead use `migrate diff --from-empty --to-schema-datamodel` + `migrate resolve --applied`."
    "Then ALSO switch the workflow off db push, restore a db:deploy script (prisma migrate deploy), and re-point db:reset at `migrate reset --force`. Adopting the files without switching the workflow is the failure mode above."
    "Tracked as a gate in PLAN.md Phase 2 (deploy path)."
  ]

  @current_workflow [
    "npm run db:push   — prisma db push (provision / sync schema.prisma to the database). VERIFIED: reports 'The database is already in sync with the Prisma schema.'"
    "npm run db:reset  — prisma db push --force-reset && tsx prisma/seed.ts (DESTRUCTIVE: drops everything, recreates from schema, reseeds). NOT end-to-end verified — the destructive run was blocked by a safety check in the session that wrote it. The --force-reset flag is confirmed to exist in prisma 5.22.0 and both halves are individually known-good, but run it once yourself before relying on it."
    "npm run db:seed   — tsx prisma/seed.ts (world-only seed, no test users; ends by calling assignNpcOwnership)"
    "npm run db:migrate — prisma migrate dev. Present for the adoption path above; do NOT use it casually while migrations are deferred, as it will generate a baseline."
    ".gitignore keeps `!server/prisma/migrations/**/*.sql` ready so the blanket *.sql rule cannot swallow migrations when they are adopted."
  ]
}

