@ai_resilience {
  description: "3-layer AI failure resilience system. Game never stops when AI is down."

  @moderation_recheck_queue {
    description: "S7 (2026-10-07): how far the moderation fail-open actually reaches. `moderationGate` publishes on an `unavailable` verdict and queues a re-check; that promise is only as good as the queue, and the queue could drop it silently."
    file: "server/src/services/aiService.ts"
    the_queue: "ONE retry queue shared by SEVEN callers (moderation re-check, NPC mail, ambient content, darknet discovery, aiOutputValidator, safeExecute, darknetDiscovery). RETRY_QUEUE_MAX=20, RETRY_MAX_AGE_MS=10min, RETRY_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3."
    why_it_was_sharp: "The failure modes are CORRELATED. `unavailable` only happens during an AI outage, and an AI outage is exactly when the queue fills with everything else that just failed — so the one entry whose loss means unreviewed player content stays published was the most likely to be evicted, precisely when it mattered."
    fixes: [
      "QueuedRequest gained `critical?: boolean`; only queueModerationRecheck sets it. Overflow now evicts the first NON-critical entry (findIndex + splice) instead of plain shift()."
      "All four give-up paths (overflow, age purge, max attempts, max attempts after throw) route through one private `abandon(req, reason)` chokepoint. The age purge previously discarded entries with NO log and NO counter at all."
      "New metric `moderationRechecksAbandoned`, ERROR-level log when a critical entry is abandoned. getMetrics() spreads this.metrics, so it reaches the admin health endpoint with no extra wiring."
      "`await onVerdict(...)` MOVED OUT of the parse try/catch. It sat under a bare `catch {}` commented \"the content simply stays visible\" — true for a parse failure, catastrophic for the other case it also caught: a correct UNSAFE verdict whose hide/notify action threw. Verdict right, enforcement lost, nothing logged. CLAUDE.md bug shape #1."
    ]
    honest_statement: "SUPERSEDED 2026-10-07 by @admin_escalation below. Was: 'content can still end up published and never reviewed; it just can no longer happen silently'."
    @admin_escalation {
      decision: "Maintainer, 2026-10-07: an abandoned re-check goes to the ADMIN REVIEW QUEUE."
      shape: "Filed as a SYSTEM report into the EXISTING queues admins already read — MessageReport via `admin reports mail`, PostReport via `forum reports` (system-wide) and the forum's own queue. No schema change, no new UI. Reason prefixed `[auto-moderation]`."
      mechanism: "moderateBeforePublish takes a REQUIRED `escalate` callback (the compiler named all 3 call sites). A QueuedRequest is `critical` exactly when it carries `onAbandoned` — nothing can be marked critical without saying where it goes when dropped. AIService.abandon() runs it; failures of the escalation itself count as `moderationEscalationsFailed`."
      paths_now_escalated: [
        "queue overflow (only if every entry is critical), age purge, max attempts, max attempts after throw"
        "re-check answer with no JSON / illegible verdict / unparseable JSON"
        "UNSAFE verdict whose hide throws — both on the immediate path and on the re-check (a forum post with isHidden=false is still LISTED even though its broadcast was suppressed)"
        "moderation service unresolvable at publish time — previously published with NO re-check and NO record"
        "re-check could not even be queued"
        "graceful shutdown: lifecycle awaits escalatePendingModeration() after stopping the timer and BEFORE db.disconnect(); includes the in-flight entry"
      ]
      named_gaps: "A CRASH (kill -9) loses the in-memory queue — graceful shutdown is covered, a crash cannot be. And an escalation whose own DB write fails (counted, logged at ERROR). Closing the crash gap would mean filing a pending report at publish time and auto-resolving it on a clean verdict — durable, but it puts every outage-time message in the admin queue. Not done; raise if crashes become a real concern."
      also_fixed: "utils/systemUser.ts — getSystemUserId was a find-then-create on a @unique username (concurrent first calls -> P2002); now an upsert, shared by messageService and forumService."
      harness: "verify-phase7-s7-moderation-queue.ts — 30 checks; S7-9 round-trips a real report through getMessageReports / getSystemReports with fixtures deleted by id; S7-10 is STRUCTURAL (shutdown ordering) because a harness cannot run a real shutdown. Six negative controls, one per mechanism."
    }
    harness: "server/scripts/verify-phase7-s7-moderation-queue.ts — 8 behavioural checks against the real queue (not greps). Negative-controlled: each of the three fixes reverted individually, each went red for its own reason."
    gotcha: "Harnesses that call setupContainer() never drain the event loop. End with `process.stdout.write(\"\", () => process.exit(fail > 0 ? 1 : 0))` or run-verify.sh kills them at its 300s timeout and scores them a FAILURE."
  }

  @layer_1_error_state {
    description: "AIService.generateResponse() returns {success, response, error}. All 12 callers (30+ call sites) check success before parsing. No more silent JSON parse failures."
    file: "server/src/services/aiService.ts"
  }

  @layer_2_smart_fallbacks {
    description: "When AI fails, faction-voiced templates provide contextually appropriate content. Game world keeps moving."
    file: "server/src/utils/aiFallbacks.ts"
    fallbacks: [
      "Welcome/departure/promotion messages — faction-voiced (garrison=military, dothackers=leet, cybercorp=corporate, darknet=cryptic)"
      "Action decisions — weighted random (leaders→issue_mission 50%, GM→plant_clue 40%)"
      "Persona replies — in-character templates per faction"
      "Forum posts — from FACTION_MUNDANE_THEMES"
    ]
  }

  @layer_3_retry_queue {
    description: "Failed AI requests queued for background retry. When AI recovers, original work completes."
    config: "Max 20 queued, 30s interval, 3 attempts, 10min TTL, 1 concurrent"
    coverage: "18 queueForRetry() calls across 9 services"
    services: [
      "PersonaService (7): follow-up messages, forum posts, clue files"
      "PersonaActionService (3): real AI actions, mission title updates"
      "MessageService (1): real AI persona reply"
      "TutorialService (1): AI hint follow-up"
      "StoryMissionService (1): step narrative update"
      "DarknetDungeonService (2): riddle update, lore files"
      "ForumService (1): NPC forum posts"
      "MissionGenerator (1): full AI mission"
      "DarknetDiscoveryService (1): AIDA recruitment DM"
    ]
    skipped: "StoryProgressionService — events stay unprocessed, naturally retry next evaluation cycle"
  }
}

