@planning_docs {
  AUDIT_2026-08-30.md: "Full 7-dimension audit — findings with file:line, severity, and a Corrections section listing claims that did NOT survive verification"
  PLAN.md: "Remediation plan. Phases 0-9 + 6b. Starts with a DECISIONS LOG (8 entries) — read that first, it governs everything else"
  SHELL_DESIGN.md: "Shell/console architecture: lexer→parser→expander→executor. §10a is the cd/ls navigation audit (N1-N10). §12 open decisions."
  KNOWLEDGE_DESIGN.md: "Knowledge & redaction progression. contentRedaction.ts is COMMITTED (confirmed by git ls-files), not uncommitted. Its real signature is redactSensitiveContent(content, options?: {skipRedaction?, cryptoSkill?}) (contentRedaction.ts:85-94) — isHomeServer is NOT a parameter; it is folded into a caller-computed skipRedaction. Core insight still holds: redaction has NO record of what a player earned, so reveals don't persist. Adds KnowledgeTopic + PlayerKnowledge (3 levels: unknown / category-known / revealed). Routes the 3 EXISTING minigame generators by topic tier as the earn mechanic — no new minigame code. SCHEMA HAS ALREADY LANDED (schema.prisma:1779, :1807); only the gameplay wiring (Phase 8) is pending."
  VERIFY.md: "WRITTEN — the file exists (256 lines). Manual playthrough checklist. With tests deferred to Phase 7, this is the only regression net."
}

@decisions_2026_08_30 {
  description: "Governing decisions. Mirrors PLAN.md's decisions log — keep both in sync."
  d1_data: "Dev/local only, no live players → migration baseline regenerable, schema changes free, no reconciliation phase"
  d2_tests: "NO automated tests until Phase 7 — codebase changing shape too fast. Gates are manual (VERIFY.md) + static CI."
  d3_phase7_tests: "Phase 7 uses CHARACTERIZATION tests written AT Phase 7, black-box, immediately before each refactor"
  d4_multiplayer: "Shared world, mostly-solo play, PLUS contested objectives/PvP/contests → Phase 3 concurrency prioritized by what is CONTESTED or SELF-RACING, not blanket-hardened"
  d5_audience: "Shallow entry, deep ceiling. Full shell ungated, discoverability via man+hints. Every objective solvable simply AND elegantly; elegance rewarded with STEALTH (calculateEvidence already scales with time-on-box), not just speed."
  d6_keybindings: "Shell semantics win when input focused; app shortcuts move to Ctrl+Shift+*. Full map in SHELL_DESIGN.md §12.1. Fixes R13."
  d7_tokenizer: "The shell tokenizer IS the G8 fix — Phase 9 Tier 1 pulls forward into Phase 1. No interim parseFlags helper."
  d8_scaleout: "Single-instance is a supported constraint for now; redis stays installed pending Phase 8's formal call."
}

@audit_2026_08_30 {
  description: "Full 7-dimension audit. Full report in AUDIT_2026-08-30.md; remediation in PLAN.md. This section records CURRENT BROKEN STATE per rule_2 — delete each entry as it is fixed."
  verdict: "OBSOLETE AS WRITTEN — re-audited against source 2026-09-24. The infrastructure half still holds (error handling, shutdown, CSRF, lockout, path sanitization, logging). 'Core GAME LOOP is non-functional' is NO LONGER TRUE: G1-G7 all have fixes in source. G1 objective dispatch, missionService.ts:808-823 (completion is sticky). G2 accept-state guard, missionService.ts:586-609. G3+S2 shop FK mismatch, shopService.syncCatalogToDatabase:678-722 run at boot (index.ts:112-113) plus the parseQuantity range check (shopCommands.ts:22-28). G4 access-level formulas and owner bypass, serverService.ts:1022-1028, 1051-1054, 1072-1074. G5 home-server read gate, networkTopologyService.ts:713-724 — see the G5 entry below for the full verified chain. G6 matchesEntity, missionIntegration.ts:32-48. G7 aiOutputValidator stepBody/branch, aiOutputValidator.ts:346-351, 357-361. STILL OPEN as of 2026-09-24, and these are what the verdict should now name: (1) search_files has NO ownership filter — aiAgentTools.ts:191-215 builds where={type,content} plus an optional serverId and returns a 200-char preview, so the agent loop can read any file's content; (2) prompt injection by REPLAY — messageService.ts:1380-1386 builds conversationLines from RAW pm.content while only :1396-1397 sanitizes, so the current turn is clean and the replayed history is not; (3) aiService.processRetryQueue has no reentrancy guard (aiService.ts:378-400); (4) [CLOSED 2026-09-24 by R10, commit cbe3fe9 — scrypt is now ASYNC via the single implementation in utils/contentCrypto.ts (await scrypt at :68,:105,:128); the four scryptSync sites are gone]; (5) safeAI hardcodes silent:true (safeExecute.ts:397), so AI failures never log at error; (6) App.svelte:55 reconnect() is a dead path — reconnect() calls disconnect(), which sets socket=null (socket.ts:152), before deferring connect() by 100ms, so getSocket() at :58 is always null and the whole if(socket) block including setUserId(:80) never runs; (7) N8 — no tree and no find commands exist; (8) N10 — ls -l still falls back to the literal string 'rwxr-xr-x' (systemCommands.ts:235)."

  @p0_game_loop_broken [
    "FIXED 2026-08-30 (G1): updateObjective now derives semantics from the RUNTIME TYPE OF target (number=count, boolean=flag), not objective.type — the declared union matched zero of the 200+ pool entries. Pool targets are only ever number (75) or boolean (59). Callers pass ABSOLUTE values not deltas (missionIntegration.ts:255,565,570). Completion is sticky. MissionObjective.type widened to string + metadata field added for G6."
    "FIXED 2026-08-30 (G2): acceptMission required 'assigned' which NOTHING writes. Canonical lifecycle is available → active → completed/failed/expired ('active' is what all missionIntegration filters test). Now accepts 'available', still honours 'assigned', and accepting an already-active mission is an idempotent no-op."
    "FIXED 2026-08-30 (G3+S2, same change): the shop LISTS from in-memory SHOP_CATALOG (18 items) while ShopItem held 15 DIFFERENT seeded rows (seed_*) — the sets were DISJOINT, so everything visible was unbuyable (P2003 on the required InventoryItem FK) and everything stored was invisible. Added ShopService.syncCatalogToDatabase(), an idempotent upsert run at boot from index.ts — chosen over fixing the seed because the catalog is CODE, so a new entry can never again be unbuyable. S2 guard added at BOTH the command layer (parseQuantity: rejects negative/zero/NaN/non-integer, caps at 1000) and inside purchaseItem+sellItem (the service is the security boundary). Verified: boot logs synced:18, 37 rows total, `buy x -1000000` rejected."
    "FIXED 2026-08-30 (G3 follow-up, visibility) — was a LIVE bug, initially understated. Missions ACTIVELY AWARD 6 legacy items today: missionService.ts:1297-1321 grants faction tokens BY NAME and missionTemplatePool.ts:1052,1774 lists them in reward.items. Rewards resolve via findFirst on NAME, which matches seed_* rows, so the grant succeeded and getPlayerInventory then filtered it out — mission completed, reward silently vanished. Fix was contained: getPlayerInventory already loads the row via include:{shopItem:true} and discarded it on a catalog miss; added fromDbRow() adapter + fallback. Verified the catalog sync introduced NO name collisions (0 duplicates across 37 rows), so reward-by-name stays unambiguous."
    "FIXED (G3 follow-up, purchasability) — verified 2026-09-24. The decision recorded here was taken the first way: 9 hardware parts and 6 persona tokens were folded into SHOP_CATALOG, ending the two-item-universe split, and prisma/reconcileShopItems.ts now runs at boot (index.ts:120) immediately after shopService.syncCatalogToDatabase() (index.ts:113), so the catalog and the ShopItem table are reconciled on every start. Ownership IS installation for hardware (maxStack 1, non-consumable, so no schema change was needed); supersession trades in at 50% inside the purchase transaction. Guarded by verify-shop-contract.ts (10/10) and verify-g3-hardware.ts (19/19), which assert hardware<->spec parity in both directions and BAN name-substring matching."
    "FIXED 2026-08-30 (G4): canAccessServer both formulas corrected, curve grounded in ACTUAL DATA (queried: encryptionLevel spans 0-5 across 44 servers, ServerLink.requiredAccess gates on 0/2/3/5, new player = level 1 / hacking 10). requiredLevel = enc * LEVEL_PER_ENCRYPTION(2) → 1/2/4/6/8/10. accessLevel = clamp(floor(hacking/10) - enc, 0, 10) → start player gets 1 on open server, maxed player gets exactly 5 on enc-5 (clears the top link gate). Balance constants named at module level. CAUGHT DURING VERIFY: needed an owner bypass (ownerId === userId → full access) BEFORE the level check, else new players would be locked out of their own home (created with encryptionLevel 1 at routes/auth.ts:116 while player is level 1). Tutorial safe — all 5 Training servers are encryptionLevel 0."
    "FIXED 2026-08-30 (G5) — RE-VERIFIED END TO END 2026-09-24, because a later audit pass wrongly re-opened this by reading canAccessServer in isolation. The chain, read directly from source: (1) home servers are created WITHOUT an accessMethod at routes/auth.ts:110 and gameStateManager.ts:948, so they inherit the schema default 'hackable' (schema.prisma:228) — NOT 'open'. (2) checkServerAccess grants only on ownerId === userId (the old `server.isPlayerHome ||` operand is gone — networkTopologyService.ts:713-724), then falls through to `case 'hackable'`, which requires a prior ServerConnection with accessLevel > 0 and otherwise DENIES; the switch's default fails closed (S11). (3) BOTH entry paths consult it: the terminal path calls it at networkCommands.ts:749 and ENFORCES at :753 with an ACCESS DENIED box, and the socket path calls it at gameStateManager.ts:590 inside authorizeServerAccess, which ANDs it with canAccessServer (:582) and fails closed on exception. canAccessServer's own three gates ARE weak (online / owner / level >= enc*2), but it is never the only gate. Conclusion: no player can read another player's home server. Anyone re-deriving this from canAccessServer alone will reach the wrong answer — that partial-path reasoning is exactly the trap CLAUDE.md warns about."
    "FIXED 2026-08-30 (G6): all 7 sites now use a matchesEntity() helper reading metadata (serverId/fileId/threadId/recipientId) instead of objective.target, which templates set to the placeholder `true`. Semantics: STRICT when bound (provisioned missions must match exactly), PERMISSIVE when unbound — required because contact_player and forum_reply are never provisioned (provisionMissionInfrastructure returns early for missions needing no server), and it keeps missions completable if provisioning failed. String targets still honoured. missionIntegration.ts:667 left alone — target===true is a genuine 'any faction' sentinel there."
    "FIXED 2026-08-30 (G7) — THREE blockers, not two: (1) validateStoryArcPlan filtered steps on s.description while the prompt asks for narrativeBrief → every step dropped → null regardless of AI quality. Now accepts description/narrativeBrief/brief/summary. (2) successBranch/failureBranch kept only if typeof string, but the prompt explicitly allows a STEP NUMBER to jump ahead → all numeric branching discarded, arcs degraded to linear chains. Now accepts string or number. (3) NEWLY FOUND: the expectedFormat retry hint passed to safeAI advertised 'description' while the prompt asked for narrativeBrief — every retry pushed the model TOWARD THE WRONG SHAPE. Rewritten to mirror the prompt. Story missions are now also registered in playerProgress.missionProgress as 'active' (matching the tutorial path — a story step is pushed by the narrative, not browsed from a board)."
    "SUPERSEDED — this is G8, and it was fixed by the Phase 1 shell tokenizer two entries below (shared/shell/ lexer+parser+args, wired through commandProcessor.tryShellParse). Flags are now separated from positionals in ls/rm/cp/mv; `ls -l`, `ls -a` and `ls -la` were verified working end-to-end over the real socket path by verify-tutorial-altpath.ts. Kept only as history — do not read it as a live defect."
  ]

  @p1_security [
    "SUPERSEDED — fixed in exactly the place this entry prescribed, so both paths inherit it. gameStateManager.authorizeServerAccess now ANDs serverService.canAccessServer (:582) with networkTopologyService.checkServerAccess (:590) and fails closed on exception (:596-602); connectPlayerToServer consults it before touching session state. Phase 4's review closed two follow-ons that this fix exposed: handleServerConnect was ignoring the returned boolean (presence was broadcast for a server the player had been denied), and the previous connection was being torn down BEFORE authorization, so a refused connect evicted the player from the server they were legitimately on."
    "SUPERSEDED — fixed as S2, landed together with G3 exactly as this entry instructed, and in BOTH layers: parseQuantity rejects negative/zero/NaN/non-integer and caps at 1000 (shopCommands.ts:22-28), and purchaseItem/sellItem re-validate inside the service, which is the real security boundary. Verified: `buy x -1000000` is rejected."
    "adminCommands.ts:388/507 — ban/kick emit force:disconnect but there are ZERO client listeners; also io.emit (global) leaks banned userId + reason to everyone. Socket auth cache never re-checks, so bans are unenforceable."
    "FIXED 2026-08-30 (S4): three controls, because DE-DUP ALONE DOES NOT CLOSE IT — the 15 distinct tool keywords sum to +2.23 success, still pinning the 0.95 clamp. (1) de-dup in parseTools AND in calculateToolBonus (the accumulating method must not trust callers). (2) OWNERSHIP via new HACK_TOOL_ITEMS map in gameBalance.ts — needed because the vocabularies were never aligned (passwordcracker vs password_cracker, zero_day vs zero_day_exploit), so a naive name lookup would reject legitimately owned tools. 11 of 15 map; keylogger/vpn/custom_backdoor/anonymizer have NO purchasable item and are deliberately omitted. Fails closed if shopService is unavailable. (3) aggregate ceiling MAX_TOOL_SUCCESS_BONUS/MAX_TOOL_STEALTH_BONUS = 0.30 each. Rejected tools now produce an explicit error naming unowned vs unrecognized. Verified: repeat-one-tool-x5 went +1.00/+2.00 → +0.20/+0.30; all 15 tools +2.23/+1.15 → +0.30/+0.30; single owned tool unchanged."
    "aiAgentTools.ts:194 search_files has no ownership filter → player `upload` content reaches the Architect loop → architectInterventionExecutor.ts:607 casts reward `as any`. Probabilistic (200-char preview), rated HIGH not CRITICAL."
    "STILL OPEN — re-verified 2026-09-24, with the citation and the count corrected. messageService.ts:1380-1386 builds conversationLines from RAW pm.content, while only :1396-1397 sanitizes originalSubject/originalContent: the CURRENT turn is sanitized and the replayed HISTORY is not, so sending two messages still gets raw text into the prompt. sanitizeForPrompt is now wired at 6 sites across 5 files (was 4)."
  ]

  @p1_data [
    "OVERTAKEN BY A LATER DECISION — corrected 2026-09-24: there is NO server/prisma/migrations directory at all (verified by ls). Migrations were deleted by maintainer decision and the project runs entirely on `prisma db push`; db:reset is `db push --force-reset && tsx prisma/seed.ts`. The .gitignore exception survives but has nothing to track, and there is no migration_lock.toml because there are no migrations. Migration adoption is deferred until a live DB exists — treat the D2/Phase 3 gate item as fully open, and treat schema.prisma as the only schema truth."
    "SUPERSEDED — there is no 0001_baseline file and no migrations directory, so there is nothing that can drift; the artifact this describes does not exist. Only the last clause survives and is still true: the project runs entirely on `prisma db push`."
    "FIXED (Phase 3 D3, passes 1 and 2) — re-verified 2026-09-24 with ZERO bypasses. Mission state lives in PlayerMission + PlayerMissionObjective and every write goes through PlayerMissionRepository; the only remaining direct touch of the old blob is auth.ts:104 writing an empty {} at row creation. Trap worth carrying forward: the repository's two mutators have DIFFERENT skip protocols — mutateAll's callback must RETURN TRUE or the write is silently discarded (playerMissionRepository.ts:305-306), whereas mutate takes a NO_CHANGE symbol sentinel (:85, :273-287), where a falsy return is a type error rather than a silent discard."
    "HALF FIXED — verified 2026-09-24. The findUnique guard is gone: the check IS the write now, inside the transaction, via PlayerProgressRepository.spendCredits(userId, total, tx), whose balance test lives in the WHERE of the decrement so the affected rowcount IS the authorization (shopService.ts:1094-1108). The old `// Re-check credits inside transaction to prevent race conditions` comment was a lie and is why nobody looked again. STILL OPEN: there is no CHECK(credits>=0) — schema.prisma:122 is a bare Int @default(1000). That one is deliberately deferred with D4 until migrations are adopted, since it needs raw SQL."
    "FIXED — verified 2026-09-24. grantRewards is entirely relative now: addCredits / increment / addExperience through PlayerProgressRepository (missionService.ts:1329-1372). No absolute value computed from a read taken outside the lock survives on this path."
    "FIXED (Phase 3) — both uniques exist in schema.prisma (:1315 and :316) and were proven to reject. Caveat recorded during D7 and still true: the FileSystemNode unique does NOT cover root nodes, because parentId is null there and NULLs are distinct — which is why the two real provisioning paths use a deterministic id `root_<serverId>` and let the PRIMARY KEY resolve the race. A partial index is the proper fix and waits on migration adoption."
  ]

